window.CET4_ARTICLES=[{"day":1,"title":"An Island Worth Protecting","theme":"海岛发展与环境保护","wordCount":354,"english":["On the tenth anniversary of their student union, a diverse group of graduates returned to a small island off the southern coast. Some had come from inland cities, while others lived near the seaside. They met on the beach, sat on an old bench by the shore, and watched fishing boats sail home. Although their jobs and opinions were different, the place seemed to unite them. The shared memory created a bond strong enough to make their separate lives feel like part of one universe.","The celebration began beside an ancient fountain at the foundation of a mountain path. Everyone wore a formal uniform for a short procession, but the mood soon relaxed. A local band agreed to perform, and a young historian explained how the island’s unusual rock formation had shaped village life. Her talk had a profound effect on the visitors. At sunset, they raised their glasses for a toast to friendship, service, and the people who had protected the island for generations.","The gathering was not free from controversy. A proposed tourism reform would involve building a large hotel, and officials had tried to formulate the plan in a business-friendly format. They promised to inform every resident and notify them before construction. Yet the environmental cost was already noticeable. Some villagers felt pressure to conform, while others held a contrary view and threatened to revolt. Their anger was not nasty or unreasonable; it came from fear that quick profit would destroy a home they loved.","Instead of allowing the meeting to reverse into a bitter quarrel, the graduates suggested a versatile solution. They would convert an empty warehouse into a visitor centre, allowing local tourism to evolve without replacing traditional life. In contrast to the hotel plan, this project would mix modern services with village customs, blend education with recreation, and create a healthy mixture of income sources. It began to stir fresh hope. Volunteers would bend bamboo, twist rope, and bind wooden frames to repair the building. Others would mount an exhibition about the sea. By making every effort revolve around the community, the project could unify development and protection."],"translation":["在学生会成立十周年之际，一群背景各异的毕业生回到了南部海岸外的一座小岛。有些人来自内陆城市，另一些人则生活在海边。他们在沙滩上相聚，坐在岸边的一张旧长椅上，看着渔船扬帆归来。尽管大家的职业和观点各不相同，这个地方似乎又把他们团结在一起。共同的记忆形成了一种牢固的纽带，让彼此分开的生活仿佛仍属于同一个世界。","庆祝活动在一条山路起点旁的古老喷泉边开始。大家穿着正式制服参加了简短的游行，不过气氛很快便轻松起来。当地乐队同意登台演出，一位年轻的历史学者讲述了岛上独特的岩层结构如何塑造村庄生活。她的讲述给来访者留下了深刻影响。日落时，人们举杯祝愿友谊、奉献精神以及世代守护这座小岛的人们。","这次聚会并非毫无争议。一项旅游改革方案计划建设大型酒店，官员们试图以有利于商业的形式制定计划。他们承诺向每位居民说明情况，并在施工前发出通知。然而，环境代价已经十分明显。一些村民感到自己被迫顺从，另一些人则持相反观点，甚至扬言反抗。他们的愤怒并非恶意或毫无道理，而是担心眼前利益会毁掉他们深爱的家园。","毕业生们没有让会议倒退成激烈争吵，而是提出了灵活的解决办法：把一座空仓库改造成游客中心，使当地旅游业能够发展，同时不取代传统生活。方案将现代服务与村庄习俗相结合，把教育和休闲融为一体，并创造多元而健康的收入来源。这一想法重新激起了希望。志愿者将弯曲竹材、拧紧绳索并捆牢木架来修缮建筑，其他人则会举办海洋展览。让所有努力都围绕社区展开，发展与保护便能得到统一。"]},{"day":2,"title":"The Path That Brought a Village Back","theme":"乡村振兴与文化保护","wordCount":null,"english":["At dawn, several young people from an ancient mountain community gathered below a high ridge. Each descendant wished to honour an ancestor who had built the stone path, and every generation of their offspring had helped protect it. Eagles seemed to soar above the valley as the group began to ascend. The exact amount of work ahead was unknown: they had to descend into a remote village first, because road access did not extend beyond the river.","A memorial procession would precede the repair project. A troop of local volunteers stood in a static line until the drums set everyone in motion. After the ceremony, the leader explained the process and safety procedure. No one could proceed alone on the damaged path. They had to remove loose stones, and the team would move supplies in a fixed ratio so that no load would exceed a safe weight.","The village had suffered during the recent recession. Visitor numbers had begun to recede, shops held excess goods, and several families considered leaving. Officials had to concede that earlier plans had failed. After a long debate, they offered a concession to small businesses and reached a compromise with conservationists. The proposal was rational rather than emotional: promote tourism, but limit construction. This was exactly the balance residents wanted, and the actual cost was lower than expected.","The motive behind the project was not profit alone. Its success would motivate young people to remain active in community life and behave responsibly toward the land. Schools planned a promotion to activate student interest, while residents would react quickly to reports of damage. Strong emotion was natural, but practical action mattered more. If the first team could succeed, a successor would lead the next stage, and a clear succession plan would keep the work alive. The village hoped to excel not by changing its identity, but by protecting it while moving forward."],"translation":["黎明时分，几位来自古老山村的年轻后代聚集在一道高高的山脊下。他们的祖先曾在那里修建石路，世世代代的子孙都参与保护它。鹰仿佛在山谷上空翱翔，队伍开始向上攀登。他们尚不清楚确切的工作量；大家必须先下到一个偏远村庄，因为道路过河后便无法通行。","道路修复前将举行纪念游行。一队当地志愿者起初整齐地静立着，鼓声响起后，所有人才行动起来。仪式结束后，负责人说明了工作流程和安全步骤。任何人都不能独自在受损小路上前进。松动的石块必须清除，物资也要按固定比例搬运，以免任何一份负重超过安全标准。","这个村庄在最近的经济衰退中遭受了困难。游客数量开始减少，商店积压了过量商品，几户人家甚至考虑搬走。官员不得不承认过去的计划失败了。经过长时间讨论，他们向小企业作出让步，并与环保人士达成妥协。新方案强调理性而非情绪：促进旅游，但限制建设。这正是居民想要的平衡，实际成本也低于预期。","这一项目的动机并不只是赚钱。项目成功能够激励年轻人积极参与社区生活，并以负责任的方式对待土地。学校计划开展宣传活动，调动学生兴趣；居民也会对道路损坏报告迅速作出反应。强烈情感很自然，但实际行动更加重要。如果第一支队伍能够成功，继任者将负责下一阶段，明确的接续计划会使工作延续下去。村庄希望通过保护自身特色并继续前进来取得出色成果。"]},{"day":3,"title":"Rebuilding Memory After the Fire","theme":"文化遗产保护与数字技术","wordCount":null,"english":["When a flash of lightning struck an ancient temple, a small flame quickly grew into a massive fire. A sudden flare lit the sky, and smoke began to fill the empty hall. Firefighters arrived to rescue two workers before the heat could injure them. The danger was real: a fragile wooden framework supported the roof, and only a fraction of it remained secure. Every accurate decision mattered because lives and a priceless piece of history were at stake.","After three consecutive days of work, experts entered the ruins. They found each fragment, however obscure, and recorded its exact position. A portion of a stone figure still showed human flesh, while traces of coloured powder and a faint fragrance survived near an altar. Curious students watched conservators mix flour with traditional materials for a temporary repair. Some visitors would frown at such a simple method, but it had actually been used for centuries.","Money soon became a problem. The current budget covered only a small proportion of the cost, and foreign currency donations could not be spent immediately. A modern architect proposed a virtual model of the building. With up-to-date equipment, the team could show how the temple had changed with fashion and how its design differed from contemporary structures. The digital project attracted numerous volunteers; messages seemed to multiply, and an abundant mass of photographs arrived from families around the region.","The work was exhausting. One volunteer offered a shoulder massage during a break, and another brought food to refresh the team. Yet the project was deeply fulfilling. Their goal was not merely to accomplish a technical task or achieve public attention. They hoped to fulfill a duty to the past and help local culture flourish. Innumerable small efforts turned a nearly lost monument into a full record of community memory. The virtual reconstruction could never replace the original, but it transformed an empty space into a shared reality."],"translation":["一道闪电击中一座古庙后，小火苗迅速发展成大火。突然的火光照亮天空，烟雾开始充满空荡的大殿。消防员及时赶到，在高温伤人之前救出了两名工人。危险十分真实：脆弱的木质框架支撑着屋顶，而其中只有一小部分仍然稳固。由于生命和无价的历史遗产都处在危险之中，每一个准确判断都至关重要。","连续工作三天后，专家进入废墟。他们寻找每一块碎片，无论多么不起眼，都记录其准确位置。一尊石像的一部分仍能看出人体形态，祭坛附近还留下彩色粉末和淡淡香气。好奇的学生看着文物修复者把面粉和传统材料混合，进行临时修补。有人可能会对这种简单方法皱眉，但它实际上已经沿用了数百年。","资金很快成为问题。现有预算只能承担一小部分费用，外币捐款也无法立即使用。一位现代建筑师提出制作建筑的虚拟模型。借助最新设备，团队可以展示寺庙怎样随时代风尚变化，以及它的设计与当代建筑有何不同。数字项目吸引了众多志愿者，信息不断增加，各地家庭还送来了大量老照片。","修复工作令人疲惫。休息时，一名志愿者为同伴按摩肩膀，另一人送来食物让大家恢复精神。然而，这项工作很有成就感。他们的目标不只是完成技术任务或获得关注，而是履行对历史的责任，让地方文化重新繁荣。无数细小努力把一座几乎消失的古迹变成完整的社区记忆记录。虚拟重建无法取代原物，却让空白之处变成了可以共同感受的现实。"]},{"day":4,"title":"When the Alarm Rang","theme":"公共安全与应急管理","wordCount":null,"english":["The manager of a large recreation centre did not realize how quickly small risks could accumulate in the realm of public safety. She would calculate visitor numbers each month and mark safety checks on a calendar, but she had begun to assume that routine paperwork was enough. When business was quiet, staff would resume old habits. They would presume every consumer understood local custom, while each customer or private client expected an agent from the booking agency to solve any problem. Visitors could consume refreshments in several halls, which created further cleaning and safety duties. Such confidence was dangerous.","One afternoon, an alarm sounded after smoke appeared near a storage room. People felt fear as the bell rang fiercely, and the possible threat began to frighten children. Some visitors fell into panic; others looked uneasy or anxious. Clear information helped ease the tension. A bright sign showed the nearest exit, while a flashing signal guided people downstairs. The manager had to assign staff to each door and add her signature to the incident report. She refused to resign, but accepted that significant change was essential. Better training was indispensable and further drills were necessary; another emergency was not inevitable, but preparation could not wait.","The city appointed an independent officer to examine the centre. His report did not simply disappoint the management. It explained how the building could accommodate elderly visitors and people with disabilities, and how staff should adapt when one exit was blocked. The centre decided to adopt a new emergency plan, appoint floor leaders, and test equipment every week.","Safety training did not have to be dull. In one exercise, actors tried to amuse children while another volunteer pretended to be lost. A sudden sound could amaze or startle participants, teaching them to remain calm. Games became a useful pastime, and recreation helped younger visitors remember the rules. However, roles were never given randomly, and no arbitrary order could replace careful planning. The team would alter each exercise, offer an alternative route, and shift people between tasks. With swift action and regular practice, the centre became both safer and more welcoming."],"translation":["一家大型休闲中心的经理没有意识到，小风险会多么迅速地积累。她每月都会计算访客人数，并在日历上标注安全检查时间，却渐渐以为日常文书工作已经足够。生意清淡时，员工又会恢复旧习惯。他们想当然地认为每位消费者都懂当地惯例，而每位顾客或私人客户则期待预订机构的工作人员解决所有问题。这种自信其实很危险。","一天下午，储藏室附近出现烟雾，警报随即响起。铃声急促作响，人们感到害怕，潜在威胁也吓哭了一些孩子。部分访客陷入恐慌，另一些人显得不安或焦虑。清晰的信息缓解了紧张情绪。醒目的标志指出最近出口，闪烁的信号灯引导大家下楼。经理安排员工守住各个门口，并在事故报告上签名。她没有辞职，却承认重大改变必不可少。更好的培训不可或缺，进一步演练也十分必要；事故并非不可避免，但准备工作不能再拖延。","市政府任命一名独立官员调查该中心。他的报告不只是让管理层失望，还说明建筑应怎样接待老年人和残障人士，以及当某个出口受阻时，员工应如何调整。中心决定采用新的应急方案，任命楼层负责人，并每周检测设备。","安全培训并不一定枯燥。在一次演练中，演员设法逗孩子开心，另一名志愿者则假装迷路。突然的声响可能使参与者惊讶或受惊，从而训练他们保持冷静。游戏成为有用的消遣，娱乐活动也帮助年幼访客记住规则。不过，角色绝不会随机分配，任意命令也不能取代周密计划。团队会调整每次演练，提供备用路线，并轮换人员任务。凭借迅速行动和定期练习，中心变得更加安全、更加友好。"]},{"day":5,"title":"The Night the Coast Went Dark","theme":"极端天气、清洁能源与社区韧性","wordCount":null,"english":["Weather on the coast can vary within minutes, and every variable makes forecasting difficult. A computer model may help experts modify a warning, but technology is invariably imperfect. During one unusually violent storm, a modest fishing town faced an earnest test. Residents were used to moderate rain and could tolerate strong wind, yet this time the sky offered almost no light and became slightly darker each minute.","A teacher tried to enlighten her students about storm safety just as lightning crossed the sky and thunder shook the windows. A solar lamp gave a brightness similar to sunlight and helped calm the room. The children felt delight when a rescue team arrived, and their parents were delighted to see them safe. Outside, however, the town’s plight was serious. Salt water threatened to blight farmland, a spark could ignite damaged wires, and birds struggled to alight. From dawn to sunset, emergency broadcasts continued to highlight safe routes.","Engineers built a solid barrier and worked to consolidate weak sections. Floodwater carried both fluid waste and clean liquid from broken pipes. Teams measured its volume, set a minimum safe distance, and marked the maximum level on a wall. A rescue vessel moved through the flood while a medic checked each patient’s pulse. Acting on impulse could be dangerous, and one impulsive volunteer cut his hand. Although he began to bleed, little blood was lost. Pumps kept one shelter dry; inside, a child watched a bubble rise beside an emergency bulb.","Small acts became a powerful gesture of unity. Banks agreed to delay each damaged family’s mortgage, and volunteers used games to engage frightened children. Psychologists explained that cognitive stress may prevent people from thinking clearly or recognizing danger. The experience taught everyone to recognize climate change as a shared challenge. When the national flag was raised over the repaired school, it represented more than recovery. The town’s local effort had become part of a global search for safer communities and cleaner energy."],"translation":["海岸地区的天气可能在几分钟内发生变化，每一个变量都会增加预报难度。计算机模型能够帮助专家修改预警，但技术总会存在不足。在一次异常猛烈的风暴中，一个普通渔镇面临严峻考验。居民习惯了中等强度的降雨，也能忍受强风，但这一次天空几乎没有亮光，而且每分钟都在变暗。","一位教师正向学生讲解风暴安全知识，闪电突然划过天空，雷声震动窗户。一盏太阳能灯提供了类似阳光的亮度，使教室平静下来。救援队到达时，孩子们十分高兴，父母看到他们平安也感到欣慰。然而，镇外的困境仍很严重。海水可能毁坏农田，火花可能点燃受损电线，鸟儿也难以降落。从黎明到日落，应急广播不断强调安全路线。","工程师建起坚固屏障，并加固薄弱部位。洪水夹带破裂管道流出的废液和清水。救援人员测量水量，规定最低安全距离，并在墙上标出最高水位。救援船穿过洪水，医护人员检查每位患者的脉搏。冲动行事可能很危险，一名冲动的志愿者割伤了手。虽然伤口流血，但失血不多。水泵使一个避难所保持干燥，里面的孩子看着应急灯泡旁升起的气泡。","一个个小行动成为团结的有力表示。银行同意推迟受灾家庭的房贷，志愿者用游戏吸引受惊的孩子。心理学家解释，认知压力会妨碍人们清晰思考或识别危险。这段经历使大家认识到，气候变化是共同挑战。修复后的学校升起国旗时，它所代表的不只是灾后恢复。小镇的地方行动已经成为全球建设安全社区、发展清洁能源努力的一部分。"]},{"day":6,"title":"More Than a Grain Festival","theme":"粮食安全与国际合作","wordCount":null,"english":["Farmers from across the globe met at an international grain festival to discuss the future of wheat. At night, lamps seemed to glitter and glow above the square; their glowing circles made glass decorations sparkle, while stars appeared to twinkle overhead. A dancer moved with grace in a graceful traditional costume. The elegant performance had great charm, and its music gave the evening an agreeable flavour. It soon became the favourite event of many visitors.","The festival also gave public honor to agricultural scientists. One eminent researcher had achieved extraordinary results with drought-resistant crops. Her prominent role and outstanding service brought glory to her team, and the audience called the award a glorious moment. In her speech, she asked governments to favour small farms. Her remark left a strong mark on listeners: progress should be measured not only by production, but also by fairness. Many described the idea as remarkable and said she spoke remarkably well.","The next day, a food-security congress sought consensus on regional cooperation. Each delegate represented a national parliament, while a senator and a city council member joined the discussion. A screen displayed a countdown to the final vote. Experts had to count available supplies, although the possible effects of climate change seemed uncountable. An accountant presented a detailed account of costs, then compared it with a counterpart from another country.","Debate was sometimes aggressive. One commentator made a sharp comment and began to digress from the main issue. The chair chose to delete a personal attack from the record and counter false claims with evidence. Delegates then considered what families encounter when food prices rise. They proposed a transport discount for remote areas and a fund that farmers could repay gradually. Everyone agreed that wasting food while others went hungry would be disgraceful. The final agreement was modest, but it turned celebration into practical action."],"translation":["来自世界各地的农民参加了一场国际粮食节，共同讨论小麦的未来。夜晚，广场上方的灯光闪烁发亮，明亮的光圈使玻璃装饰熠熠生辉，星星也在头顶闪耀。一名舞者身穿优美的传统服装，动作从容。典雅的表演富有魅力，音乐也为夜晚增添了宜人的韵味，很快成为许多游客最喜欢的活动。","节日还向农业科学家致敬。一位著名研究人员在抗旱作物方面取得了非凡成果。她的重要作用和杰出贡献为团队带来荣誉，观众称颁奖时刻十分光荣。她在演讲中呼吁政府支持小农场。她的一句话给听众留下深刻印象：衡量进步不能只看产量，也要看公平。许多人认为这一观点意义非凡，并称赞她讲得格外出色。","第二天，粮食安全大会寻求就地区合作达成共识。每位代表来自本国议会，一位参议员和一名市议会成员也参加讨论。屏幕显示最终投票的倒计时。专家需要统计现有物资，尽管气候变化的潜在影响似乎难以计数。一名会计提交了详细费用账目，并与另一国家的同行进行比较。","辩论有时十分激烈。一名评论员发表尖锐意见，并开始偏离主要议题。主席决定从记录中删除人身攻击，并用证据反驳错误说法。代表们随后讨论家庭在食品涨价时会遇到的问题。他们建议为偏远地区提供运输折扣，并设立农民可以逐步偿还的基金。所有人都认为，一边浪费食物、一边让他人挨饿是可耻的。最终协议虽然有限，却把庆祝活动转化成了实际行动。"]},{"day":7,"title":"Saving the Park, Rebuilding Trust","theme":"城市公共空间与廉洁治理","wordCount":null,"english":["A neglected park lay beneath the city skyline. Its lawn had become a field of weed, every bush needed a brush with gardening tools, and one corner looked like a jungle. The city faced a large repair bill, but an earlier loan had left it in debt. With a growing budget deficit, officials warned that the project could make the district nearly bankrupt. Yet residents argued that a healthy public space was worth saving.","The park had to undergo major repairs after years of poor care and could not endure another wet season. Paths meant to be durable had begun to deteriorate; rain would erode the soil, wooden seats would decay, and rubbish would spoil the pond. Children suffer when play areas fall into ruin. Experts said the work’s duration could be reduced if fertile soil and safe fertilizer were used wisely.","Planners presented a new outline and layout. The design would underline the stream that seemed to underlie the park’s original shape. Some residents prefer a modern style, while others wanted a different plan and appeared indifferent to appearance. Everyone agreed that outdated equipment and stale water must go. A strict deadline would determine whether public funds remained available.","At a public conference, engineers would confer with residents and refer technical questions to an independent referee. From the evidence, citizens could infer why costs had risen and perceive a deeper problem: a corrupt contractor had offered a bribe. People began to whisper that false records were intended to deceive inspectors and cheat taxpayers. The news threatened to disrupt the meeting; angry voices could erupt and interrupt every speaker. However, the chair refused to let anger undermine the discussion. Transparent accounts and open debate finally gave the park—and public trust—a chance to recover."],"translation":["城市天际线下有一座长期无人管理的公园。草坪已变成杂草丛生的荒地，每片灌木都需要用园艺工具清理，一个角落甚至像丛林。修复费用高昂，而此前的贷款又使城市背上债务。面对不断扩大的预算赤字，官员警告该项目可能让这一地区接近破产。然而，居民认为，健康的公共空间值得挽救。","公园多年缺乏维护，已经无法再承受一个雨季。原本耐用的小路开始破损；雨水侵蚀土壤，木椅逐渐腐烂，垃圾污染池塘。游乐区成为废墟，孩子们也因此受影响。专家表示，如果合理使用肥沃土壤和安全肥料，工程持续时间可以缩短。","规划人员提交了新的提纲和布局。设计将突出那条似乎构成公园原始形态基础的小溪。一些居民更喜欢现代风格，另一些人希望采用不同方案，还有人对外观漠不关心。大家一致认为，过时设备和不新鲜的积水必须清除。严格的期限将决定公共资金能否继续使用。","在公开会议上，工程师与居民协商，并把技术问题交给独立评审员。根据证据，市民可以推断成本上升的原因，并看出更深层的问题：一家腐败承包商曾试图行贿。人们开始低声议论，虚假记录意在欺骗检查人员、欺诈纳税人。消息几乎扰乱会议，愤怒的声音随时会爆发并打断发言。但主持人没有让愤怒破坏讨论。透明账目和公开辩论最终让公园和公众信任都有了恢复机会。"]},{"day":8,"title":"What the Harbour Revealed","theme":"港口安全、环保清理与数据调查","wordCount":null,"english":["A young engineer was asked to conceive a low-cost system for cleaning an old harbour. The control screen was blank when she first entered a vacant office, and a blanket of fog covered the water outside. An unused pipe worked like a vacuum, pulling waste from places where factories used to dump it. Instead of telling workers to discard everything as trash, she planned to separate material that could be recycled.","The project became urgent after a collision between two cargo boats. A clash over radio instructions led one vessel to crash into a wall and crush a small platform. The wreck did not smash the main fuel tank, but repairs required more cash than expected. The captain felt ashamed and made a dash to help injured workers. Investigators hoped the accident would advance safety reform, improve training, and persuade officials to approve new rules. Clear proof could enhance public trust, enlarge the cleanup programme, and enrich future research.","Before each trip, crews had to fasten every rope, keep containers tight and watertight, and check that nothing was loose. They learned how to undo a damaged lock, enclose chemicals safely, and keep emergency tools in a marked closet. Each cable hung from a secure hook. Companies also had to disclose what they carried, seal every box, and never conceal a dangerous substance. Honest records would reveal risks and help inspectors uncover illegal trade.","On the day of the test, workers began to load sensors onto a boat. At sea, they could download maps, upload readings, and unload equipment quickly. As the trip began to unfold, the new materials proved able to withstand waves from a distant storm. Constant communication continued through three successive trials, and the results remained consistent. An instant warning appeared when oil touched a sensor; the response was almost instantaneous. The harbour was not clean yet, but reliable information had turned a hopeful idea into practical progress."],"translation":["一名年轻工程师构想出一套低成本的旧港口清理系统。她第一次走进空置办公室时，控制屏幕一片空白，外面的水面被浓雾笼罩。一根废弃管道像吸尘器一样，把过去工厂倾倒在隐蔽处的废物吸出。她没有让工人把所有东西都当垃圾丢弃，而是计划分拣可以回收的材料。","两艘货船相撞后，项目变得十分紧迫。无线电指令上的冲突导致一艘船撞上港墙，压坏一个小平台。残骸没有砸破主油箱，但维修所需现金超过预期。船长感到羞愧，立即冲去帮助受伤工人。调查人员希望事故能推动安全改革、改进培训，并促使官员批准新规定。明确证据能够增强公众信任、扩大清理计划并丰富后续研究。","每次出航前，船员都要系紧绳索，确保容器严密、防水，并检查是否有松动。他们学习怎样打开损坏的锁、妥善封装化学品，并把应急工具放进有标识的储物柜。每根电缆都挂在牢固的钩子上。企业还必须公开货物信息，封好每个箱子，绝不能隐瞒危险物质。真实记录可以揭示风险，帮助检查人员查明非法交易。","测试当天，工人开始把传感器装上船。在海上，他们可以下载地图、上传读数并快速卸下设备。航程逐步展开时，新材料证明能够经受远处风暴带来的海浪。三次连续试验中，通信始终不断，结果也保持一致。油污一接触传感器，警报便立即出现，反应几乎是瞬间完成的。港口尚未完全清洁，但可靠信息已经把一个充满希望的想法变成实际进展。"]},{"day":9,"title":"Beneath the Mountain","theme":"矿难救援与安全责任","wordCount":null,"english":["A sudden blast in a mountain mine prompted an immediate rescue. People in a nearby apartment building were told to depart, while the emergency department kept families apart from the danger zone. Dust filled the air, and each particle made breathing difficult. Early reports were only partial. To remain impartial, officials warned journalists against prejudice and bias and asked them to use neutral language until the facts were clear.","Several miners had acute injuries, and two were in severe, even grave, condition. Further movement underground could aggravate their wounds. Doctors worked to alleviate pain, relieve pressure, and organize relief supplies. Families began to grieve, yet remained grateful when the government agreed to grant extra medical support. Rescue teams had to grind and polish a damaged metal door before it could open. Another pipe might burst, a trapped gas pocket could explode, and every careless tear in protective material created risk.","An experienced explorer led the team through an old passage. He had spent years learning how to explore the region and knew how companies sometimes exploit valuable land without proper safeguards. Water began to shed from the rock like rain. In one chamber, his lamp caught a crystal beside a miner with a dusty beard. The stone looked like treasure, but human life was far more precious. The team had no time to appreciate its beauty.","After the rescue, investigators had to evaluate the mine and estimate the cost of repair. They refused to devalue workers’ lives by treating safety as a minor expense. Their ultimate aim was prevention, and ultimately the company accepted stricter rules. Engineers made an approximate map—approximately three kilometres of tunnels—and had to reckon with the fact that one reckless decision had caused the accident. An intimate knowledge of the mine’s origin, rock structure, and ventilation organ was essential. The final report showed that prompt action saves lives, but responsible management must prevent disaster in the first place."],"translation":["山区矿井突然发生爆炸，救援工作立即展开。附近公寓楼的居民被要求撤离，应急部门则让家属远离危险区域。空气中布满尘埃，每一个微粒都让呼吸更加困难。最初报告并不完整。为保持公正，官员提醒记者避免偏见，并要求在事实明确前使用中立语言。","几名矿工受了急性伤害，其中两人伤势严重，甚至情况危急。井下进一步移动可能加重伤情。医生努力减轻疼痛、缓解压力并组织救援物资。家属开始悲痛，但政府同意提供额外医疗援助时，他们仍心怀感激。救援队必须打磨损坏的金属门才能打开它。另一根管道可能爆裂，受困气体可能爆炸，防护材料上的任何裂口都会带来风险。","一位经验丰富的探险者带领队伍穿过旧通道。他多年勘察该地区，了解企业有时会在缺乏安全措施的情况下开发宝贵土地。水珠像雨一样从岩石上落下。在一个洞室里，他的灯照到一块水晶，也照到一名满脸尘土、留着胡须的矿工。石头看起来像宝物，但生命更加珍贵，队伍无暇欣赏它的美。","救援结束后，调查人员需要评估矿井并估算维修费用。他们拒绝把安全当作小开支，从而贬低工人的生命。最终目标是预防事故，公司最终也接受了更严格的规定。工程师绘制了大致地图，隧道约三公里长，并判断一次鲁莽决策导致了事故。深入了解矿井的起源、岩层结构和通风装置十分必要。报告表明，迅速行动可以救命，但负责任的管理必须首先防止灾难发生。"]},{"day":10,"title":"A Safe Home for Rare Birds","theme":"野生动物保护与公众教育","wordCount":null,"english":["A wildlife reserve was created beside a forest reservoir where several rare birds reside. Scientists believed the species might originate in the northern hills and derive its strength from a varied diet. If logging continued, it would deprive the birds of the habitat they needed to thrive. A thriving population required residents to strive for balance between work and conservation. In accord with local custom, every resident could still gather fallen wood near a residence, regardless of income.","Researchers kept a careful record and treated every animal with regard. They studied what insects the birds eat, where they inhabit the forest, and whether their instinct helps them avoid danger. A sharp thorn could pierce a wing, a bee might sting, and a sudden storm could thrust a nest from a tree. Trained observers learned to distinguish ordinary movement from distress. One distinguished observer made a distinct discovery: each bird had a distinctive warning call.","Fire was the greatest risk. Rangers placed an extinguisher at every station and practised how to extinguish flames before they spread. A new regulation required visitors to observe marked paths. Conservative estimates suggested that without protection the species could become extinct. The reserve therefore worked to conserve water, preserve old trees, protect nesting areas, prevent disturbance, and shield young birds from noise. Cameras could detect illegal entry, while a volunteer detective checked reports of traps or poison.","The education centre used scent to make learning memorable. A fragrant local flower inspired a natural perfume, but guides warned that pleasant smells do not prove a plant is safe. Some plants contain poison. Rules forbid visitors to pick them, and a complete ban may prohibit entry during breeding season. In return, the centre would exhibit photographs and feathers in an annual exhibition. The birds deserve more than admiration: they need informed observation, patient care, and a community willing to protect the conditions in which life can continue."],"translation":["一座野生动物保护区建在森林水库旁，几种珍稀鸟类栖居在那里。科学家认为，这一物种可能起源于北部山区，并从多样食物中获得力量。如果砍伐继续，鸟类将失去赖以繁衍的栖息地。种群要兴旺，居民就必须努力在工作与保护之间取得平衡。按照当地习惯，无论收入多少，每位居民仍可在住处附近收集落木。","研究人员认真保存记录，并重视每一种动物。他们研究鸟类吃什么昆虫、栖息在森林何处，以及本能是否能帮助它们避险。尖刺可能刺穿翅膀，蜜蜂可能蜇伤它们，突如其来的风暴也可能把鸟巢从树上掀落。受过训练的观察者学会区分普通活动与求救行为。一位杰出的观察员有了明确发现：每种鸟都有独特的警报叫声。","火灾是最大风险。护林员在每个站点放置灭火器，并训练如何在火势蔓延前扑灭火焰。新规定要求游客停留在标记道路上。保守估计表明，如果缺少保护，该物种可能灭绝。因此，保护区努力节约水源、保存古树、保护筑巢区，并使幼鸟免受噪声干扰。摄像机可以发现非法进入，志愿调查员则核查陷阱或毒物报告。","教育中心利用气味增强学习效果。一种芳香的本地花卉启发人们制作天然香水，但导游提醒大家，好闻并不代表植物安全，有些植物含有毒素。规定禁止游客采摘，繁殖季甚至可能完全禁止进入。作为回馈，中心将在年度展览中展出照片和羽毛。鸟类值得的不只是欣赏，还需要科学观察、耐心照料，以及愿意保护生命延续条件的社区。"]},{"day":11,"title":"The Museum the Storm Could Not Silence","theme":"海洋文化遗产保护与青年就业","wordCount":322,"english":["A seaside museum planned to display the town's marine heritage in a former submarine station. A light breeze entered through a cracked window, but workers had to squeeze large photographs into a compact hall. As dark clouds emerged, the temperature began to freeze the wet floor, and rising water threatened to submerge the entrance. The staff stopped to gaze at the harbour; one glance at the tide gave them a glimpse of an emergency, while the glare of lightning made everyone stare in silence.","The alarm reminded the director to recall an earlier flood that had damaged a monument. She sent a memo from memory, ordered one warning shot from a signal gun, and called the fire service. The museum employed twenty local people. Every employee knew the emergency plot, and their employer protected employment by arranging a nearby flat as a temporary office.","The crisis came during inflation. Ticket prices could not be inflated, yet a dense wall needed repair and the density of visitors made evacuation difficult. Staff condensed the exhibition, watched the crowd shrink, and refused to let public interest fade. The storm had a serious impact and could influence tourism; an influenza outbreak had already reduced income. Even so, volunteers exerted themselves. Fluent guides from affluent families worked beside residents for whom money was scarce and help was scarcely available.","Rare objects were moved first, although such pieces were rarely shown. One family had inherited an old compass whose value was inherent in its story. A guide's fluency helped explain that it represented a shared heritage, not merely property for an heir. By morning, the museum was safe, and the community had protected both its past and its future jobs. After the storm, the museum did not simply reopen. It raised electrical equipment, marked safer escape routes and invited fishermen to review the new flood plan. Their knowledge of local tides corrected several assumptions made by outside engineers."],"translation":["一家海滨博物馆计划在旧潜艇站展示小镇的海洋文化遗产。微风从破窗吹入，工作人员则要把大幅照片安排进紧凑的展厅。乌云出现后，湿地面开始结冰，涨水也可能淹没入口。大家望向港口；潮水的一眼便让他们察觉紧急情况，闪电的强光更令众人一时沉默。","警报使馆长想起早先的一次洪水，那次灾害曾损坏一座纪念碑。她凭记忆发出通知，让信号枪鸣响一次，并联系消防部门。博物馆雇用了二十名本地居民。每位员工都熟悉应急方案，雇主还租下附近公寓作为临时办公室，以保住大家的工作。","危机恰逢通货膨胀。门票不能随意涨价，可密实的墙体需要修缮，拥挤的人流也让疏散更困难。工作人员压缩展览内容，看到人群逐渐减少，却不愿让公众兴趣消退。暴风雨严重影响旅游业，而此前的流感也已削减收入。尽管如此，志愿者仍全力以赴，家境富裕、表达流利的讲解员与缺少资金和帮助的居民并肩工作。","珍稀物品最先被转移，尽管它们平时很少展出。一个家庭保存着祖传罗盘，其价值本来就存在于背后的故事中。它代表共同遗产，而不只是留给继承人的财物。到清晨，博物馆转危为安，社区也同时守住了过去与未来的工作机会。暴风雨后，博物馆并没有简单地重新开放，而是抬高电气设备、标明更安全的逃生路线，并邀请渔民审查新的防洪方案。他们对本地潮汐的了解纠正了外来工程师的几项错误判断。"]},{"day":12,"title":"A Climate Camp with Common Sense","theme":"气候教育、生态保护与乡村课堂","wordCount":290,"english":["At an international youth convention, the atmosphere became tense when an intensive climate workshop began. Students had an intense sense of responsibility, but a few senseless claims upset sensitive listeners. A sensible teacher asked everyone to use common sense and reject nonsense: melting ice was a real warning, yet fear alone could not tame the problem.","The group visited a tropical wetland, an important source of water and a resource for local families. Protecting it was fundamental to both physical and mental health. A fatal loss of one species could affect the total system. Students used digital maps, and a talented guide explained why clean water was vital. Their task was to attain reliable knowledge, record each attainment, retain useful data, and maintain the instruments.","The camp also had to entertain younger pupils. Its entertainment combined creative games with scientific creation. To sustain interest, every activity had to pertain to daily life. Students obtained clay, built concrete models, and were briefly detained by a storm rather than arrested by boredom. They learned that every species and creature, from bacteria to humankind, had a place. A humble artist used humor to explain why humid air, tropical heat, a sudden chill, moist soil and a damp wall could damage a cottage.","Before leaving, the class rendered the evidence as a short film. It showed that human creativity cannot replace nature, but it can help people understand it. The students returned home determined to protect the wetland with facts, patience and practical action. Back at school, each group chose one habit it could measure for a month, such as electricity use or food waste. The results were modest, but they taught students to distinguish a hopeful slogan from a change supported by evidence."],"translation":["一次国际青年会议举行气候专题活动时，现场气氛一度紧张。学生责任感强烈，但少数毫无道理的说法让敏感的听众不安。一位理性的教师提醒大家运用常识、拒绝胡言：冰层融化确实是警告，但恐惧本身无法解决问题。","团队参观了热带湿地。它既是重要水源，也是当地家庭赖以生存的资源，对身心健康都具有基础意义。某一物种的致命损失可能影响整个系统。学生使用数字地图，一位有才华的向导说明清洁水源为何至关重要。他们要获得可靠知识、记录成果、保留有效数据并维护仪器。","营地还要让低年级学生乐于参与，因此把科学创造与趣味游戏结合起来。为了保持兴趣，每项活动都要联系日常生活。学生取来黏土，制作混凝土模型；暴风雨让他们暂时受困，却没有让他们因无聊而放弃。他们认识到，从细菌到人类，每个物种和生物都有自己的位置。一位谦逊的艺术家用幽默讲解潮湿空气、热带高温、突然降温和湿墙怎样损坏村舍。","离开前，大家把证据制作成短片。作品说明，人类创造力不能取代自然，却能帮助人们理解自然。学生带着事实、耐心与实际行动的决心回到家中。回到学校后，每组选择一种可以连续测量一个月的习惯，例如用电量或食物浪费。结果并不惊人，却让学生学会区分充满希望的口号与有证据支持的真实改变。"]},{"day":13,"title":"The Science Fair That Corrected Itself","theme":"校园科学展、健康教育与语言规范","wordCount":306,"english":["At a school science fair, each individual joined a team, and teachers took care not to divide or subdivide pupils by gender. Male and female students shared the mainstream event in the main hall, while smaller groups used a side stream of classrooms. A scream came from the food lab when cream and butter boiled over. Steam rose, water began to evaporate into vapour, and a stain appeared and then seemed to disappear.","The accident changed the appearance of one poster but did not make the evidence vanish. It explained how bacteria, a virus and a germ spread. The writer had typed immine, a mistaken form, where immune was intended. The balance of the report was good: parallel charts presented an apparent paradox without turning the fair into a parade or march of claims about paradise, heaven or hell.","Outside, a safe haven held plants and insects. A barber volunteering at the gate lifted a heavy box with a heave and found a bug and a worm beneath it. Wooden signs warned visitors not to desert the area or confuse desert with dessert. In a language booth, students learned to assert a point, insert a quotation and recognise that exsert was an unusual form. A judge asked why the mistaken spelling had not been removed before opening day. The students answered that leaving a clearly labelled correction allowed visitors to see how scientific work improves: errors are recorded, examined and repaired rather than quietly hidden.","The final project concerned a tree transplant. International students helped translate instructions and transmit data through a transparent network. Moving the tree would transform the yard, but transport costs required a careful transaction and a fair transfer of funds. By correcting its own errors openly, the fair taught a lesson larger than any prize: reliable learning grows through cooperation and revision."],"translation":["学校科学展中，每位学生都加入团队，教师也注意不以性别划分学生。男女生共用主展厅，小组活动则分流到旁边的教室。食品实验室忽然传来尖叫，原来奶油和黄油煮沸溢出。蒸汽升起，水分蒸发成水汽，一块污迹出现后又似乎消失。","小事故改变了海报外观，却没有让证据消失。海报讲解细菌、病毒和病菌怎样传播。作者误把 immune 写成了 immine，大家及时标明这是拼写错误。报告其余部分结构均衡：平行图表展示了一个表面悖论，并未把科学展变成关于天堂或地狱的夸张口号游行。","室外区域为植物和昆虫提供安全环境。一名在门口做志愿者的理发师费力搬起箱子，发现下面有虫子和蚯蚓。木牌提醒访客不要擅自离开，也不要混淆 desert 与 dessert。语言展台则教授如何明确主张、插入引文，并说明 exsert 是一个罕见形式。一名评委问，为什么不在开放日前删掉那个拼写错误。学生回答，保留并明确标注更正，可以让参观者看到科学工作如何进步：错误应被记录、检查和修正，而不是悄悄隐藏。","最后一个项目是移植树木。国际学生协助翻译说明，并通过透明网络传输数据。移树会改变校园，但运输费用需要谨慎交易和公平转账。科学展公开修正自身错误，让大家懂得：可靠学习来自合作与反复改进。"]},{"day":14,"title":"A Harvest Plan Everyone Could See","theme":"乡村丰收、公共信息与社区规划","wordCount":316,"english":["A village council rejected an opaque development plan and demanded apparent, obvious and evident reasons for every decision. Evidence soon began to loom over the debate: a tourism boom could help local flowers bloom, but careless building might bring gloom and leave farmers gloomy. Leaders should boost incomes without boasting about results that had not arrived.","The harvest committee compared raw vegetables with crude products, waited for fruit to become ripe, and taught students how to reap grain after ploughing. A mature farm should yield food while keeping soil healthy. No dominant voice called a farmer dumb for asking questions. Residents with weak immune systems needed safe meals, and domestic animals required care. Even a dull or tedious chore followed a schedule, a scheme, an agenda and a daily routine.","The chosen transit route passed through an old passage whose interior needed repair, although its exterior looked sound. External media praised the project, but an internal review found problems. The local newspaper became a useful medium between experts and residents, while intermediate reports stopped rumours. Officials used a website to locate each site, record its location, allocate money and situate new stalls away from traffic. To test the plan, two student reporters walked the entire route at dawn and interviewed shopkeepers before the market opened. Their notes revealed a dangerous crossing that no official map had shown.","At the final meeting, speakers changed their posture from defence to cooperation. They did not pose as perfect leaders; instead, they showed maps, admitted uncertainty and invited questions. The result was a harvest plan that protected farmland, supported visitors and allowed everyone to see where public money would go. The council also promised to publish a short report after the harvest. It would compare expected income with actual earnings and show whether traffic, water use and rubbish had increased. Future decisions would then rest on results, not celebration speeches."],"translation":["村委会拒绝了一份不透明的发展方案，要求每项决定都给出清楚、明显且有证据的理由。争论中逐渐显现一个事实：旅游繁荣能够带动本地产业开花结果，但无序建设也可能带来阴影，使农民悲观。领导者应促进增收，却不能夸耀尚未取得的成果。","丰收委员会比较新鲜蔬菜与粗加工产品，等待果实成熟，并教学生在耕地后如何收割。成熟农业既要产粮，也要保持土壤健康。免疫力较弱的居民需要安全饮食，家畜也需要照料。即使单调家务，也按照时间表、方案、议程和日常流程完成。","选定路线穿过一条旧通道。它的外部看似完好，内部却需要修缮。外部媒体称赞项目，但内部审查发现问题。本地报纸成为专家和居民之间有效的沟通媒介，中期报告也阻止了谣言。官员通过网站确定各地点及位置，分配资金，并把新摊位安排在远离车流之处。为了检验方案，两名学生记者清晨走完整条路线，并在市场开门前采访店主。他们的记录发现了一处官方地图未标出的危险路口。","最终会议上，发言者从防守姿态转向合作。他们不再装作完美领导者，而是展示地图、承认不确定性并欢迎提问。最终方案既保护农田、服务游客，也让所有人看清公共资金的去向。委员会还承诺在收获季后公布简短报告，比较预计收入与实际收益，并说明交通、用水和垃圾是否增加。今后的决定将依据结果，而不是庆祝活动上的讲话。"]},{"day":15,"title":"Designing a City for Daily Life","theme":"城市规划、城乡联系与公共交通","wordCount":322,"english":["A city planning class exposed students to a difficult choice: how should officials dispose of an old factory site? One group wanted to depose the current plan and prevent disposable buildings. It would propose a positive solution: deposit reusable materials nearby, compose a mixed neighbourhood, invite a composer to design a public space, and reuse every component in the final composition, including the fore section of the old gate.","No authority should impose a solution or oppose every opponent. The opposite position also deserved counsel. The purpose was to connect a rural county with an urban centre, a suburb, downtown streets and the wider metropolitan area. Every citizen had a civil right to join the discussion about civilization, country and countryside. A retired bus driver then drew the missing links on the map. His experience showed that a technically impressive design could still fail if it ignored the daily journeys of older residents.","Engineers studied the ground surface and wrote a preface to their report. A new bridge could surpass the old one, but workers still needed a compass when river water began to surge. The design allowed pedestrians to leap across no danger and used trees to surround homes, softening noisy surroundings. Climate, public mood and family circumstance all mattered. Buses would travel in a circle around a transport circuit so that passengers could circulate safely. To understand the proposal, students travelled at rush hour with a nurse, a shop worker and a parent taking a child to school. The same route felt completely different to each passenger, so the final design added earlier buses and a protected crossing.","The mayor promised to conduct an open review and direct funds in a clear direction. Experts would instruct contractors rather than command residents as if the project were military work. By looking forward, the class learned that good planning does not erase the past; it brings different places and people into a workable future."],"translation":["城市规划课给学生提出一道难题：旧工厂用地应如何处置？一组学生希望撤换现有方案，避免建设一次性建筑。他们提出积极建议：把可再用材料存放在附近，建设混合型社区，请作曲家参与公共空间设计，并在最终构成中重新利用每个部件。","任何部门都不应强加方案，也不能一味反对所有异议者。相反观点同样值得听取和咨询。规划目的，是把乡村县域、城市中心、郊区、市中心街道以及更大的都市区域联系起来。每位公民都有文明参与讨论城乡未来的权利。一位退休公交司机随后在地图上补出了缺失的连接。他的经验说明，再先进的技术方案，如果忽视老年居民的日常出行，也可能失败。","工程师研究地表，并为报告撰写前言。新桥可以超过旧桥，但河水上涨时工人仍需要指南针。方案不让行人冒险跳跃，也让住宅远离嘈杂环境。气候、公众情绪与家庭情况都要考虑。公交车将绕着交通环线运行，让乘客安全流动。为了理解方案，学生在高峰时段分别陪同护士、商店员工和送孩子上学的家长出行。同一条路线给每位乘客的感受完全不同，因此最终设计增加了早班公交和受保护的人行横道。","市长承诺公开审查，并把资金引向明确方向。专家会指导承包商，而不会像指挥军事行动那样命令居民。课程让学生明白，优秀规划并非抹去过去，而是让不同地方与人群共同走向可行的未来。"]},{"day":16,"title":"Restoring the Statue, Rebuilding Trust","theme":"社区合作、公共权力与历史纪念","wordCount":310,"english":["A neighbourhood decided to restore a statue of a writer who had fought for liberty. The project would liberate the square from neglect and remind residents of an earlier liberation movement. Officials deliberately avoided a hasty decision; after deliberate discussion, they set a decade-long care plan.","The author of the original monument had challenged unfair authority. The council now had to authorize repairs while proving that every material was authentic and genuine. A young design genius compared previous records with prior photographs and gave safety the highest priority. The old base was inferior, so workers chose a superior stone whose superiority was tested rather than merely described as superb or supreme. Before selecting new stone, the team placed samples outdoors through winter. Cheap material cracked after repeated rain and frost, while the stronger choice kept its colour. Publishing that test helped residents understand why the repair cost more than expected.","The committee tried to communicate openly. Mutual respect guided telecommunications with distant experts and meetings within the community. Every block in the neighbourhood could send an associate from a local association. Sociable, easy-going volunteers worked with a former rival, an ally and a new alliance of schools and businesses.","Their online network allowed residents to oversee spending and foresee delays while keeping the statue in sight. Sightseeing companies offered support, but public insight prevented commercial control. One oversight was quickly corrected when a weather forecast predicted heavy rain. From that point forth, work moved forward and its status stayed public. By reopening day, the statue did more than capture the past: it showed the community's capacity to cooperate, and even nearby cabinet, cabin, cable and cattle displays helped children connect national stories with ordinary life. At the reopening ceremony, children read short passages from the writer's work. Older residents, who had once argued over the budget, stood together and agreed to inspect the square every spring."],"translation":["一个社区决定修复一座纪念争取自由的作家的雕像。项目要让广场摆脱荒废，也提醒居民记住早期的解放运动。官员特意避免仓促决定，经过慎重讨论后制定了十年维护计划。","纪念碑原作者曾挑战不公权力。如今委员会既要批准修缮，也要确认材料真实可靠。一位年轻的设计天才把过去记录与早期照片对照，并把安全列为最高优先事项。旧底座质量较差，工人于是选择经检测更优的石材，而不是只用“极佳”或“最高级”等词宣传。在选择新石材前，团队把样品放在室外经历整个冬季。便宜材料在反复雨雪和冰冻后开裂，更坚固的材料则保持原色。公开测试结果使居民明白修复费用为何高于预期。","委员会努力公开沟通。相互尊重贯穿远程通信以及社区会议。街区可以从当地协会派代表参加。善于交往、随和的志愿者与过去的竞争者、盟友以及学校和企业组成的新联盟共同工作。","网络让居民监督开支并预见延期。观光企业愿意资助，但公众洞察避免了商业控制。天气预报警示大雨后，一项疏忽被及时纠正。重新开放时，雕像不仅留住历史，也展现社区合作能力；帐篷里的橱柜、小屋、电缆和牲畜等历史展品，还帮助孩子把国家故事与日常生活联系起来。重新开放仪式上，孩子们朗读了这位作家的作品片段。曾为预算争论的老居民站到一起，并约定每年春天共同检查广场。"]},{"day":17,"title":"A Workshop Where Every Voice Counted","theme":"青年创新、民主参与与职场规则","wordCount":310,"english":["A youth centre held a democratic workshop to show how democracy can generate practical change. A small generator powered the hall, and the general strategy was simple: each team needed a strategic plan, not a clever hack that merely hid a scratch. Students could pinch a wire, scrape a plate, consult a catalog and record their dialog before tools were scattered across the room.","The centre's constitution stated that trust must constitute the basis of teamwork. A substitute teacher from a technical institute challenged superstition and superstitious rumours. Participants of different religion, including a student whose family had lived in exile, exchanged exotic ideas without trying to expel or compel anyone.","Rules had force because the next generation of the workforce needed safe habits in every workplace and workshop. Mentors would enforce eye protection, reinforce good practice and keep a backup power supply. Yet authority was limited: willpower and willing cooperation worked better than pressure on a reluctant learner. Leaders could restrain unsafe behaviour, but restraint should not restrict imagination, create strain or constrain debate. One quiet participant noticed that the safety instructions were too technical for beginners. She redesigned them with pictures, and her version prevented mistakes more effectively than the longest speech of the day.","At the end, teams stripped old machines for parts. They learned not to rip a cable, lose their grip, paint a misleading stripe, or leave a trap near the door. To grasp a problem was more valuable than trying to grab the prize. The workshop taught that democratic innovation grows when firm rules protect people and free discussion improves ideas. The final machine was less impressive than some early designs, yet it was safer and easier to repair. Every group demonstrated one failure as well as one success, turning the exhibition into an honest account of learning rather than a competition in appearance."],"translation":["青年中心举办民主创新工作坊，展示民主怎样产生实际改变。小型发电机为大厅供电，总体策略很简单：每组都要制定有战略性的方案，而不是用小技巧掩盖划痕。学生可以夹紧电线、刮净金属板、查阅目录并记录对话，但不能把工具随处散落。","中心章程规定，信任必须构成团队合作的基础。一位来自技术学院的代课教师反对迷信及相关传言。不同宗教背景的参与者，其中还有家庭曾流亡的学生，彼此交流新奇想法，却不驱逐或强迫任何人。","规则具有约束力，因为未来劳动者必须在各种工作场所和车间养成安全习惯。导师执行护目规定、强化正确操作并准备备用电源。不过，权力也有限：意志力与自愿合作比向不情愿的学习者施压更有效。领导者可以制止危险行为，但克制不应限制想象或讨论。一位不爱说话的参与者发现，安全说明对初学者过于专业。她用图片重新设计后，比当天最长的演讲更有效地避免了错误。","最后，各组拆解旧机器回收零件。他们学会不要扯断电缆、失去控制、涂上误导性条纹，或在门边留下危险装置。真正理解问题，比只想抢夺奖品更有价值。最终机器不如某些早期设计抢眼，却更安全、更容易维修。每组既展示一次失败，也展示一次成功，使展览成为对学习过程的真实记录，而不是外观上的竞赛。"]},{"day":18,"title":"A Fair Chance to Start Again","theme":"公平招聘、职业培训与社会关怀","wordCount":320,"english":["A job centre was once a mess, and its records created chaos and disorder. A new manager introduced an orderly system so that applicants received equal treatment. She did not equate equal opportunity with identical results; instead, she offered adequate support and equivalent tests, coordinated interviews, and checked whether decisions were fair and fairly explained. On her first morning, the new manager watched applicants move through the building without interfering. One man missed an interview because two signs pointed in opposite directions. That small observation convinced her to redesign the process from the visitor's point of view.","The centre treated unemployment as a public affair as well as a business problem. It helped a factory abolish abusive questions and prevent the abuse of personal data. Visitors could wander through a career fair, stroll past training booths, enroll in a course, check payroll information, or take a trolley to a recruitment event. Employers agreed to recruit by skill and entitle qualified applicants to feedback.","A qualification could be shown with a receipt, while each recipient met a receptionist who helped register an entry. Services also supported a pregnant worker, a parent after divorce, and people struggling to concentrate because they had indulged an addiction. A dictionary exercise asked learners to contradict a false claim, deny a rumour, predict an outcome and indicate the evidence.","The improved facility admitted its own defects and measured their effect on applicants. Staff understood how anxiety could affect affection within families or infect a workplace with distrust. Local manufacturers sought perfect workers, but the ideal candidate did not exist. A thorough review looked at the whole person. The centre's lesson was simple: a fair chance combines clear standards with practical help. Six months later, the centre compared the new records with the old ones. More applicants had completed training, and complaints had fallen, but staff still invited unsuccessful candidates to explain where the process felt unclear."],"translation":["一家就业中心过去十分混乱，杂乱档案造成工作失序。新经理建立有条理的系统，让求职者得到平等对待。她没有把机会平等简单等同于结果相同，而是提供充分帮助和同等测试，协调面试，并检查决定是否公平、解释是否清楚。新经理上任第一天早晨没有急着干预，而是观察求职者如何在楼内办理事务。一名男子因两块指向相反的标牌错过面试。这个细节使她决定从访客角度重新设计流程。","中心把失业视为公共事务，也视为企业问题。它帮助工厂废除带有侵犯性的提问，防止滥用个人数据。访客可以逛招聘会、浏览培训展位、报名课程、查询工资信息，或乘有轨车前往招聘活动。雇主同意按技能招聘，并让合格申请人有权得到反馈。","资格可以凭证明材料确认，每位服务对象都由接待员帮助登记。中心还帮助孕期员工、离异后的父母，以及因沉迷成瘾行为而难以集中注意力的人。词典练习要求学员反驳错误说法、否认传言、预测结果并指出证据。","改造后的机构承认自身缺陷，并评估这些问题对求职者的影响。工作人员理解焦虑怎样影响家庭感情、怎样让不信任扩散到职场。制造企业都想要完美员工，但理想候选人并不存在。全面审查应看到完整的人。六个月后，中心把新旧记录进行比较。完成培训的求职者更多，投诉也减少了，但工作人员仍邀请未被录用者说明流程中哪些地方不够清楚。"]},{"day":19,"title":"From an Empty Factory to a Learning Town","theme":"战后重建、地方产业与教育振兴","wordCount":292,"english":["A deadly conflict had left a factory empty and damaged a border territory. The old laboratory, lavatory, gallery, grocery and nursery stood beside beautiful scenery, but the landscape still carried scars. A landlord offered the site to the town after troops had invaded the nearby cape. Residents feared that outsiders might intrude, or that another intruder might attack, yet a peace treaty ended the struggle before either side could conquer the former colony.","Retreat was followed by negotiation, and the agreement became a civic triumph rather than a military victory. The council negotiated with both sides, initiated repairs and set an initial budget. A student initiative helped launch the project and utilize abandoned rooms as classrooms. Not everyone welcomed the change. Some families wanted the ruins left untouched, while others urgently needed jobs. The council therefore preserved one damaged wall as evidence of the conflict and repaired the remaining buildings for public use.","People could interact without allowing political groups to interfere. Mediators intervened when arguments grew, and every interval included an open interview. A local journal followed the long journey of recovery; its journalist learned to interpret evidence instead of repeating slogans. The journal invited former soldiers, factory workers and displaced families to check its reports before publication. Their memories sometimes disagreed, so the editor printed those differences instead of forcing them into one simple account of the past.","An academic academy soon opened on the site. A visiting scholar funded a scholarship, and a seminar and public forum discussed tuition, faculty duties and the dean's role. Experts from different disciplines explained that a school needs both a responsible principal and clear principles. The transformation did not erase painful history. It gave the town a place to study it, rebuild trust and prepare a more peaceful economy."],"translation":["一场致命冲突使工厂空置，也破坏了边境地区。旧实验室、洗手间、展厅、杂货店和托儿所坐落在美丽风景旁，地貌却仍留着伤痕。军队侵入附近海角后，一位房东把场地交给小镇。居民担心新的入侵者和袭击，所幸和平条约在任何一方征服旧殖民地之前结束了冲突。","撤退之后开始谈判，协议成为公民社会的胜利，而非军事凯旋。委员会与双方协商，启动修复并制定初步预算。学生倡议帮助项目正式开展，把废弃房间利用为教室。并非所有人都欢迎改造。有些家庭希望原样保留废墟，另一些人则迫切需要工作。因此，委员会保留了一面受损墙体作为冲突见证，同时修复其余建筑供公众使用。","人们可以彼此交流，同时不让政治团体干涉。争论激烈时，调解者及时介入；每个阶段还安排公开访谈。本地刊物记录漫长复苏历程，记者学习解释证据，而非重复口号。这份刊物邀请退伍军人、工厂职工和流离失所的家庭在出版前核对报道。他们的记忆有时并不一致，因此编辑保留这些差异，而没有强行把过去写成一种简单说法。","不久，一所教育学院在原址开办。来访学者资助奖学金，研讨会和公共论坛讨论学费、教师职责与院长角色。不同学科的专家说明，学校既需要负责任的校长，也需要明确原则。改造并未抹去痛苦历史，而是让小镇拥有研究历史、重建信任并发展和平经济的场所。"]},{"day":20,"title":"The Campus Built by Its Students","theme":"大学生活、人才培养与校园建设","wordCount":298,"english":["A prince and princess once gave an unused palace to a public college, but students turned it into a real campus. During a volunteer camp, they climbed the hill and began a campaign to repair classrooms. The debate had no single champion: dormitory residents, every undergraduate from freshman and sophomore to junior and senior, and students studying for a bachelor or master's degree all contributed.","An art major restored a masterpiece, while a former dropout returned as a skilled worker. A layman learned to add a protective layer beside an amateur painter and a veteran engineer. Their sophisticated plan would nourish curiosity, cultivate responsibility, rear young trees and breed a stronger community. Students kept a public list of needed repairs and matched each job with the right level of experience. Beginners painted furniture under supervision; trained workers handled wiring and roofs. This division protected volunteers without treating inexperience as uselessness.","The college valued intelligent action as much as intellect. Intellectual honesty required people to acknowledge mistakes. A pioneer in rural education invited students to review one another as peers and choose compatible goals. The curriculum mixed chemistry with sociology: a chemical experiment was guided by a chemist, while classes in logic and geometry helped explain design.","Art students learned to articulate ideas and elaborate them through architecture. An architect showed how to construct and erect safe walls above basic infrastructure and a stable base. The project proved that education is not limited to lectures. When students share knowledge, physical work and public responsibility, an old building can become a living school. The first term brought practical results. Nursing students opened a weekend clinic, engineering students repaired the water system, and literature students recorded the memories of workers who had served the palace long before it became a college."],"translation":["一位王子曾把闲置宫殿赠给公立学院，真正把它变成校园的却是学生。志愿营期间，大家爬上山坡，发起修缮教室的行动。这里没有唯一冠军：住校生、从大一到大四的本科生，以及攻读学士或硕士学位的学生都作出了贡献。","艺术专业学生修复杰作，一名曾经退学的学生以熟练工人身份回来。外行人与业余画家、资深工程师一起学习铺设保护层。成熟方案既滋养好奇心、培养责任，也栽培幼树、塑造更有活力的社区。学生公开列出所需维修项目，并按经验水平分配工作。初学者在指导下粉刷家具，受过训练的工人负责线路和屋顶。这种分工既保护志愿者，也没有把缺少经验等同于毫无用处。","学院同样重视聪明的行动和智力。学术诚实要求人们承认错误。一位乡村教育先驱让学生以同伴身份互评并选择相容目标。课程把化学与社会学结合起来：化学家指导实验，逻辑与几何课程则帮助学生理解设计。","艺术生学习清楚表达并进一步阐述建筑理念。建筑师讲解如何在基础设施和稳固地基之上建造安全墙体。项目证明，教育不只发生在课堂讲授中。学生共同投入知识、劳动和公共责任，旧建筑也能成为充满生命力的学校。第一个学期便取得了实际成果。护理专业学生开设周末诊所，工程专业学生修复供水系统，文学专业学生则记录了那些早在宫殿改成学院之前便在此工作的人的回忆。"]},{"day":21,"title":"When the Stage Became a Classroom","theme":"校园戏剧、阅读能力与心理成长","wordCount":313,"english":["A campus drama club prepared a basic drama programme: a tragedy and a comedy about online life. At first, the plot seemed ridiculous and even absurd, but an index helped the actors track every ingredient and element of the story. The director explained that trust was a major factor: one false message could spread like paste, while a portable phone could become part of a harmful compound and a complex social problem. The director did not begin with a finished script. She asked each performer to bring a family story, then built the play from those different voices. Rehearsals became a form of research as well as artistic training.","The cast became perplexed when a stage pond began to collapse. Repairs complicated rehearsal and provoked an argument. One student advocated patience, another cracked a whip for sound effects, and a confused actor made a blunt comment. Sharp criticism can shape a performance, but personal attacks only confuse people.","The teacher used the accident to exemplify responsible speech. She quoted a line about a quest for truth and requested that students require evidence rather than demand instant agreement. The task was demanding: they had to acquire information, inquire about sources, distinguish literal meaning, and improve media literacy through literature.","The group encouraged a shy member instead of discouraging or dispiriting him. Team spirit began to inspire new ideas, and his inspiration made others aspire to perform well. Eager as an eagle, he expressed a desire to continue even after the lights expired and rehearsal had to cease. The final play showed that art can turn confusion into understanding when people listen before they judge. After the final performance, audience members stayed to discuss which scenes felt true and which seemed simplified. Their comments became material for the next version, so the stage continued to function as a classroom even after the lights went out."],"translation":["校园戏剧社准备了一部关于网络生活的悲剧和一部喜剧。最初，情节显得可笑甚至荒诞，但索引帮助演员追踪故事的每个组成部分。导演指出，信任是关键因素：一条虚假消息会像胶水一样扩散，便携手机也可能成为复杂社会问题的一部分。导演没有拿出一份写好的剧本，而是请每位演员带来一个家庭故事，再用这些不同声音构成整部戏。排练因此既是艺术训练，也成为一种调查研究。","舞台水池开始塌陷时，全体演员都很困惑。维修使排练更复杂，也引发争论。一名学生主张保持耐心，另一人挥动鞭子制作音效，一位糊涂的演员则说了生硬的话。尖锐批评可以塑造表演，人身攻击却只会让人更加混乱。","教师借事故说明负责任表达的重要性。她引用追求真相的台词，要求大家以证据为前提，而不是强求立刻赞同。这项任务并不轻松：学生要获取信息、询问来源、理解字面含义，并通过文学提高媒介素养。","团队鼓励害羞成员，而不是打击他的精神。集体精神激发新想法，他的灵感也让其他人追求更好的演出。他像鹰一样热切，即使灯光熄灭、排练被迫停止，仍希望继续。最终作品说明，人在判断前先倾听，艺术就能把困惑转化为理解。演出结束后，观众留下来讨论哪些场景真实、哪些显得过于简单。他们的意见成为下一版的素材，因此即使灯光熄灭，舞台仍继续发挥课堂的作用。"]},{"day":22,"title":"A Repair Map for Safer Streets","theme":"城市基础设施、工程技术与交通安全","wordCount":303,"english":["After a bridge was suspended from service, traffic came to a halt. Citizens subscribed to a repair newsletter and inscribed warnings on a public map. The first script was a handwritten manuscript, but engineers prescribed a clearer digital system. It required skill, technique and technology, including biotechnology sensors maintained by a technician, a technologist and a mechanic who understood the mechanism. The project began after two cyclists were injured within one week. Instead of blaming careless individuals, students compared police records, street lighting and traffic speed. The pattern pointed to a design problem near the station entrance.","A control drawer held plans for drainage. The city promised not to overdraw its budget or withdraw support. New hardware connected with radar and measured radiation near an old factory. The press called the case pressing, and public pressure increased. Officials knew that delay could depress local trade and deepen depression among shop owners.","A successful repair would impress residents, but an impressive announcement was less useful than an honest impression of risk. Depressed shop owners needed facts. Teams compressed data without repressing criticism, suppressing evidence or oppressing nearby families. They expressed results through maps of an expressway, freeway, motorway, highway, sidewalk and bypass. Every by-passer could see where construction would occur. Residents tested the map during an evening walk. A wheelchair user found two blocked ramps, while a delivery rider pointed out a corner hidden from drivers. Both observations were added before the map was published.","The final print included fingerprints on safety cards and a blueprint for the bridge. A public hearing asked whether the plan served justice. Sound judgement had to justify the cost and reject any unjustified shortcut. If disagreement reached court, a jury and fair trial could review the record. Engineering, the class concluded, is also a promise of public responsibility."],"translation":["一座桥暂停使用后，交通完全停顿。市民订阅维修简报，并在公共地图上标注警告。最初方案只是手写稿，工程师随后规定使用更清晰的数字系统。系统需要技能、技术与科技，包括由技术员、科技人员和机械师维护的生物传感器。项目始于一周内发生的两起骑车人受伤事故。学生没有简单责怪个人粗心，而是比较警方记录、道路照明和车辆速度，最终发现车站入口附近存在设计问题。","控制柜存放排水图纸。城市承诺不透支预算，也不撤回支持。新硬件连接雷达，检测旧工厂附近的辐射。媒体称问题十分紧迫，公众压力不断增加。官员明白，拖延会压低本地贸易，也会加重店主的沮丧。","成功维修会给居民留下深刻印象，但精彩声明不如诚实说明风险。团队压缩数据，却不压制批评、隐瞒证据或侵害附近家庭。他们用地图展示快速路、高速公路、人行道和绕行线，过路人都能看清施工位置。居民在一次夜间步行中测试了地图。一名轮椅使用者发现两处坡道受阻，一名送货骑手则指出一个司机看不见的转角。地图发布前，这些观察结果都被补了进去。","最终印刷品附有安全卡指纹与桥梁蓝图。听证会审查方案是否符合正义。合理判断必须说明成本依据，拒绝没有理由的捷径。若争议进入法院，陪审团和公正审判可以复核记录。工程也是对公共责任的承诺。"]},{"day":23,"title":"A Trial That Taught More Than Law","theme":"法治教育、成瘾预防与青年责任","wordCount":311,"english":["A university held a mock trial about digital crime and discrimination. A student chose to sue a company after being falsely accused. The defence offered an excuse, while the appeal team prepared to prosecute those responsible. No one was allowed to curse, place a careless charge, discharge private information, or blame a victim without proof.","The judge asked both sides not to surrender reason. The court could condemn misconduct only after lawyers verified the facts. A witness and a bystander described the event, and the jury had to decide whether to convict. Its verdict should never become a form of torture or demand an unnecessary sacrifice from an innocent family. The judge explained that a fair process may still produce an unpopular result. What matters is whether both sides can present evidence, challenge doubtful claims and understand the reasons for the decision. This distinction changed the students' debate.","Outside the courtroom, volunteers assisted a campaign against heroin. They resisted easy slogans, persisted with patient education, and agreed that prevention consists of more than punishment. The programme comprised counselling, praise for progress, and work opportunities in a social enterprise rather than dreams of a pirate empire. It addressed guilt without humiliation.","A trained mentor accompanied each participant and helped manage daily goals. The chair and student president tried to harness community support and control costs. Schools competed in a poster competition, but competent teams remembered that cooperation mattered more than team A versus team B. Workshops also warned against gambling, a casual bet, online piracy, kidnapping and prison violence. The lesson was clear: justice protects society best when law, education and support work together. After the visit, the class held a mock hearing in which students exchanged roles. Those acting as witnesses discovered how frightening public questioning could be, and those acting as lawyers learned that accuracy mattered more than dramatic language."],"translation":["一所大学举行关于网络犯罪与歧视的模拟审判。一名学生因遭到错误指控而起诉公司。辩方提出理由，上诉团队则准备追究责任。任何人都不能咒骂、随意控告、泄露隐私，或在没有证据时责怪受害者。","法官要求双方不放弃理性。只有律师核实事实后，法院才能谴责不当行为。证人与旁观者叙述事件，陪审团决定是否定罪。裁决绝不能变成折磨，也不能让无辜家庭作出不必要牺牲。法官解释，公平程序仍可能产生不受欢迎的结果。重要的是双方能否提交证据、质疑可疑说法并理解裁决理由。这一区分改变了学生们的讨论方式。","法庭外，志愿者协助开展反海洛因活动。他们抵制轻率口号，坚持耐心教育，并认为预防不只是惩罚。项目包括咨询、对进步的肯定，以及社会企业提供的工作机会，而非建立庞大势力的幻想。","导师陪伴每位参与者管理日常目标。负责人和学生主席努力汇集社区支持并控制成本。学校参加海报比赛，但有能力的团队明白合作比相互对抗重要。活动还提醒人们远离赌博、网络盗版、绑架和监狱暴力。法治、教育与支持结合，才能更好保护社会。参观结束后，班级举行模拟听证会，学生互换角色。扮演证人的人感受到公开询问可能令人害怕，扮演律师的人则明白准确比戏剧化语言更重要。"]},{"day":24,"title":"Following the Money in a Public Project","theme":"公共财政、法律责任与信息公开","wordCount":295,"english":["A guilty contractor had to kneel before the council after mud from an unsafe site entered a river. He claimed to be innocent and naive, but inspectors found that decent safety rules had been ignored. A financial incentive had encouraged speed. The council decided to execute the law, and its executive accepted no loophole.","Officials released the report and published it for the public. Companies were obliged to meet every obligation, and managers were responsible for environmental responsibility. Legal advisers reviewed legislation and each statute. Every item of evidence had to be valid and independently validated because the pollution had become a local crisis. A journalism club requested the original contracts rather than relying on a summary. By comparing dates, prices and signatures, its members found a payment entered twice. Officials corrected the record before any accusation was made.","The finance office examined commerce around the project. A commercial supplier had treated water as a commodity and hidden payments to a merchant for poor merchandise. Stock and trade records even misused a trademark. A revised budget set a cleanup target and identified tax revenue, a funding avenue, household income, gross cost and the expected outcome. When the duplicate payment was found, the club contacted the contractor before publishing its story. A simple data-entry mistake, not theft, had caused the problem. Correcting it publicly showed why careful verification should come before a dramatic headline.","The council also prepared for an outbreak of illness. A medical outlet improved its outlook and output, while teams worked to overcome delays, not overlook small risks, and avoid overnight decisions. Auditors could overtake the schedule by sharing work, but overtime bills were already overdue. Public trust returned only when the town could see both the law and the money being followed."],"translation":["一家承包商让不安全工地的泥水流入河道，负责人在委员会前跪下认错。他声称自己无辜且不知情，但检查人员发现基本安全规定遭到忽视。追求速度的经济奖励造成了问题。委员会决定严格执行法律，行政负责人不接受任何漏洞。","官员公布报告供公众查阅。企业有义务履行全部责任，管理者也要承担环境责任。法律顾问审查法规和各项法令。每项证据都必须有效并经独立验证，因为污染已成为地方危机。新闻社团没有只看摘要，而是申请查阅原始合同。成员通过比较日期、价格和签名，发现一笔款项被重复登记。官员在任何指控出现前便更正了记录。","财政部门调查项目相关商业活动。商业供应商把水当作商品，还隐瞒向商人采购劣质货物的付款。库存和交易记录甚至滥用了商标。新预算确定清理目标，列明税收、融资渠道、家庭收入、总成本和预期结果。发现重复付款后，社团在发表报道前先联系了承包商。问题源于简单的数据录入错误，而非盗窃。公开更正说明，认真核实应当先于吸引眼球的标题。","委员会还防备疾病暴发。医疗服务点改善计划与产出，团队努力克服延期，不忽视小风险，也避免一夜之间作决定。审计人员可以协作追赶进度，但加班账单已经逾期。只有法律和资金去向都清楚可查，公众信任才会回来。"]},{"day":25,"title":"A Town That Chose to Produce Less Waste","theme":"循环经济、社区互助与资源节约","wordCount":292,"english":["A local economist explained that a healthy economy is not simply about producing more. Economics can support economical choices, generous sharing and limits on greedy consumption. A repair centre could produce useful goods, reproduce spare parts, improve each product and raise productivity without expanding heavy industry.","Workers cleaned an old mould and learned to manipulate and operate safe machines. Businesses agreed to cooperate and collaborate, while a safety bar and barrier protected visitors from a barren yard full of broken barrels and buckets. At a weekend bargain market, one volunteer became embarrassed when an addition error doubled a price.","The town opened the centre with a small ceremony rather than an expensive celebration. It also held a memorial for a mechanic whose funeral had brought the community together. His workshop saved fuel, taught people to bury unsafe waste correctly, and gave young trainees reasons to cheer. They took pleasure in raising a cheeky painted dragon, used a lift rather than dragging heavy metal, and hauled parts without a roar of engines.","A harbour shed offered shelter and shade, and a barber demonstrated how to shave wood safely. What looked like a silly or artificial project could elevate local skill and address a serious problem: residents were deficient in repair experience. Training made them proficient, efficient and sufficient in number to serve nearby villages. Even a shallow change in buying habits could lower waste and strengthen the local economy. In a final language review, the class also used deficiency accurately in context. A year later, the town weighed its rubbish again. Packaging waste had fallen, repair shops had gained customers and the sharing centre was busy. Food waste remained high, however, so restaurants joined the next stage instead of declaring the campaign complete."],"translation":["本地经济学家指出，健康经济并不只是生产更多。经济学也能支持节约选择、慷慨分享，并限制贪婪消费。维修中心能够生产用品、复制零件、改善产品并提高生产率，而不必扩张重工业。","工人清理旧模具，学习安全操作机器。企业同意合作，安全栏和屏障则把访客与堆满破桶的荒地隔开。周末折扣市场上，一名志愿者因加法错误把价格翻倍，十分尴尬。","小镇用简朴仪式而非昂贵庆典开放中心，同时纪念一位已故机械师。他的工作坊节约燃料，教人正确掩埋危险废物，也让年轻学员振奋。他们升起彩绘龙，借助升降机而不生拉重物，在没有发动机轰鸣的情况下搬运零件。","港口棚屋提供遮蔽和阴凉，木工还演示安全刨木。看似不起眼的项目解决了严重不足：居民缺乏维修技能。培训让足够多的人熟练而高效地服务周边村庄。即使购买习惯只发生小变化，也能减少废物、增强地方经济。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。一年后，小镇再次称量垃圾。包装废物减少了，维修店顾客增加，共享中心也很繁忙。然而食物浪费仍然严重，因此餐馆加入下一阶段，而不是宣布行动已经完成。"]},{"day":26,"title":"The Honest Label Campaign","theme":"消费权益、产品检查与跨境贸易","wordCount":309,"english":["A consumer group asked shops to lower hidden costs. People sometimes swallow a false promise because an advertisement looks soft as a pillow, while the real guarantee is hollow. A product may bring profit and be profitable, but public benefit also matters. Every fee, bus fare, farewell gift, welfare payment, pension and allowance should be described clearly. The campaign started when a child with an allergy became ill after eating a snack whose label used unfamiliar terms. Her family did not ask for the product to be banned; they asked for information that an ordinary shopper could understand quickly.","A reporter acted like a spy only in the sense that she examined every aspect. She suspected misleading labels and reported suspicious claims to an inspector. The team inspected goods, monitored prices, respected privacy and compared results respectively. Their prospect was a market where a spectator could see conspicuous facts rather than speculate from a distant perspective through a telescope.","Trade rules also shaped prosperity. Officials marked the margin, horizon, boundary, legal bound, road bounce, platform edge, farm hedge, national frontier and container rim used in shipping. Import and export forms matched each passport. A porter, tailor, retailer, wholesaler and second-hand seller all received the same guidance. The campaign invited shoppers to photograph unclear labels and send questions to producers. Within a month, three companies rewrote their packaging in plain language, while a local supermarket created a desk where customers could compare products.","The campaign asked stores to advertise honestly. It investigated details from retail to wholesale and warned that a false label can become a reputational bomb, even when no law is broken. Trust grows slowly, but clear prices and careful inspection help buyers make choices without fear. Teachers later used the new labels in a consumer lesson, asking pupils to explain which information changed their choice and why."],"translation":["消费者组织要求商店降低隐性成本。广告可能像枕头一样柔软诱人，使人吞下虚假承诺，实际保证却十分空洞。产品可以盈利，但公共利益同样重要。各种费用、车费、告别礼物、福利、养老金和补贴都应说明清楚。这项活动源于一名过敏儿童食用标签术语生僻的零食后生病。她的家人并未要求禁售产品，而是要求提供普通消费者能够迅速看懂的信息。","记者像侦探一样审查每个方面。她怀疑标签误导，把可疑宣传交给检查员。团队检查商品、监测价格、尊重隐私，并分别比较结果。他们希望建立一个市场，让旁观者看到醒目事实，而不必隔着遥远视角凭空猜测。","贸易规则也影响繁荣。官员标出航运涉及的边距、地平线、边界、道路起伏、平台边缘、农场树篱、国境与容器边沿。进出口表格与护照一一对应，搬运工、裁缝、零售商、批发商和二手卖家都接受相同指导。活动邀请消费者拍下含糊标签，并向生产商提出问题。一个月内，三家公司用通俗语言重写包装说明，本地一家超市也设置服务台，方便顾客比较产品。","活动要求商店诚实宣传，从零售到批发都核查细节。即使没有违法，虚假标签也可能成为声誉上的炸弹。信任建立缓慢，而清楚价格与认真检查能让消费者安心选择。后来，教师把新标签用于消费教育课，请学生说明哪些信息改变了自己的选择以及原因。"]},{"day":27,"title":"Choosing a Course Without Losing Yourself","theme":"大学选课、个性发展与学习支持","wordCount":304,"english":["A student bumped into a campus notice board, damaged its bumper-like frame and found a lump beneath the paper. Enrolment was in a slump, so advisers embraced a new plan. They gave specific course specifications, explained each particular requirement particularly clearly, and listed special options, every speciality and each specialist available. Before choosing, Mei attended three trial classes and spoke with graduates rather than trusting advertisements. One course promised a quick salary but offered little practice; another was demanding, yet its students could explain exactly what they had learned.","No student was treated as a unique problem for having a peculiar, odd or weird interest. Advisers became acquainted with learners and tried not to bother, annoy or ignore them. An ignorant response to mental health can lead to neglect, even when an early sign seems negligible. Negative or passive advice may turn an optimistic student pessimistic.","The school supplied a course guide and a supplement. Learners could opt for an optional class, but basic safety training remained compulsory. For each case, they selected lectures, elected representatives and collected feedback on dialect, sector, section, segment, semester and term. Mei also calculated tuition, travel and living costs with her parents before signing any agreement.","The programme also offered outdoors study. One class used a safety brace and chose to venture on an adventure expedition, showing that education is more than sitting indoors. Choice works best when information is clear, support is kind and students accept responsibility for the path they select. In a final language review, the class also used ignorance accurately in context. In the end, Mei chose neither the cheapest course nor the one with the boldest promise. She selected a programme with supervised practice and clear assessment, while keeping a part-time job that allowed her to test whether the field truly suited her."],"translation":["一名学生撞到校园公告栏，弄坏类似保险杠的边框，还发现纸张下面有一处凸起。选课人数正在下降，顾问于是采纳新方案：提供具体课程说明，把各项要求讲得格外清楚，并列出特殊选项、专业方向和可咨询的专家。作出选择前，梅试听了三门课，并与毕业生交流，而不是只相信广告。一门课程承诺快速获得高薪，却很少安排实践；另一门虽然要求严格，学生却能清楚说明自己真正学到了什么。","学生不会因为兴趣独特、古怪或与众不同而被当作问题。顾问主动了解学习者，避免打扰、惹恼或忽视他们。不了解心理健康会导致疏忽，即使早期迹象看似微不足道。消极被动的建议也可能把乐观学生变得悲观。","学校提供课程指南和补充材料。学生可以选择选修课，但基础安全培训仍为必修。各类个案都可选择讲座、选举代表，并按方言、领域、章节、学期等分类收集反馈。签署任何协议前，梅还和父母一起计算了学费、交通费与生活费。","项目还安排户外学习。一门课组织探险考察，说明教育不只是在室内坐着。信息清楚、支持友善、学生也为自己的选择负责时，选择才真正有意义。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。最终，梅既没有选择最便宜的课程，也没有选择承诺最响亮的课程。她选择了有指导实践和明确考核的项目，同时保留兼职工作，以检验这个领域是否真正适合自己。"]},{"day":28,"title":"Tourism That Leaves a Place Stronger","theme":"可持续旅游、公共设施与健康生活","wordCount":298,"english":["During vacation, students considered tourism as a possible vocation. Their excursion included a city tour, interviews with a tourist group, a mountain journey and a short voyage. Morning yoga and a simple workout kept everyone fit, while attention to well-being made the gym and gymnasium energetic places rather than rooms that merely consumed energy. Tourism first expanded after a photograph of the lake became popular online. Coaches arrived before the village had toilets, signs or trained guides. Residents soon realised that a larger crowd did not automatically bring a better local economy.","A battery-powered display made the programme dynamic and vigorous. Visitors could see a visible route, test visibility in fog, revise a plan and discuss a long-term vision with a supervisor. Guides tried to previse risks, predict crowds and compare a forecast with visual evidence. Students then visualized the experience from the audience's view.","A deputy director helped devise an accessible device and other apparatus for older travellers. A supervisor would supervise technicians as they installed air conditioning, furnished rooms with safe furniture and decorated them with local ornaments. Better facilities should raise comfort, not arouse wasteful demand or cause prices to rise. The village limited visitor numbers on busy weekends and trained local guides instead of importing temporary staff. Part of every ticket paid for footpath repairs, rubbish collection and the protection of a nesting area near the lake.","At the end, an early bell would waken students to a wider responsibility. They concluded that good tourism helps a community arise without damaging its identity. It should awaken respect, raise local income and allow hosts and visitors to learn from one another. At the end of the season, residents reviewed both income and environmental data. Visitor satisfaction remained high, and fewer paths showed signs of damage."],"translation":["假期里，学生思考旅游能否成为未来职业。考察包括城市游览、采访游客、山地旅行和短途航行。晨间瑜伽与简单锻炼帮助大家保持健康，对身心状态的关注也让健身房充满活力，而不是只消耗能源。一张湖泊照片在网上走红后，旅游业迅速发展。旅游大巴到来时，村里还没有厕所、标识或受过培训的向导。居民很快意识到，人群更多并不自动意味着本地经济更好。","电池供电的展板让项目更具动感。游客可以查看路线、测试雾天能见度、修改计划，并与主管讨论长期愿景。导游预先考虑风险、预测人流，把天气预报同视觉证据比较，学生再从观众视角设想完整体验。","副主任协助设计方便老年游客使用的设备。技术人员安装空调，用安全家具布置房间，并以本地装饰品美化环境。更好的设施应提升舒适度，而不是刺激浪费需求或推高价格。村庄在繁忙周末限制游客人数，并培训本地向导，而不是从外地临时招人。每张门票都有一部分用于维修步道、清理垃圾以及保护湖边的筑巢区域。","考察结束时，学生意识到更大的责任。优秀旅游应帮助社区发展，同时不损害自身特色；它应唤起尊重、增加本地收入，并让主人与游客互相学习。旅游季结束时，居民同时审查收入与环境数据。游客满意度仍然很高，出现破坏痕迹的步道则减少了。"]},{"day":29,"title":"New Neighbours, Shared Stories","theme":"人口流动、社区融入与文化理解","wordCount":293,"english":["A town report began with a clear conclusion and conclusive summary: housing policy must include newcomers, not exclude or eliminate them. Everyone was welcome except those who promoted violence, and any exception required exceptional reasons. Officials should not overhear private talk, overwhelm families with forms or create an overwhelming first week.","A volunteer team agreed to undertake the overall task. Problems could occur or recur, so the town built a curb, traced service requests, followed each trail and tracked results. It also addressed idleness through work support. At a welcome meal, a shy child began to blush when juice flushed across the table and made a splash. At first, the welcome dinner was awkward because several guests spoke little Chinese. A teenager used drawings and a translation app to start a conversation, and soon the families were comparing school routines, recipes and childhood games.","The guest list recorded surname and given name, namely for practical contact rather than judgement. Services supported an infant, an adolescent, an idle youngster seeking work, and an elder living alone. Some families immigrated as immigrants, while others had emigrated or migrated within the country. Their new setting and social context shaped every story.","A friendly contest, not a protest, invited residents to share music they loved or detested. Under the moon, people discussed appetite, carpets, careers, cargo work, an old scar and a winter scarf. A vicar, a Christian family and neighbours who honoured each saint joined the same meal. The event did not erase differences; it gave people a safe way to understand them. The new neighbours later organised an open afternoon in the apartment courtyard. Children taught one another games that needed almost no language, while adults exchanged practical information about buses, clinics and local rules."],"translation":["小镇报告得出明确而有说服力的结论：住房政策必须接纳新居民，而不是排斥或清除他们。除鼓吹暴力者外，人人都应受到欢迎，任何例外都必须有充分理由。官员不应偷听私下谈话，也不应用大量表格压垮刚到的家庭。","志愿团队承担整体任务。问题可能发生或再次出现，因此小镇修建路缘、追踪服务请求并记录结果。欢迎餐会上，一个害羞孩子因果汁洒满桌面、溅得到处都是而脸红。起初，欢迎晚宴有些尴尬，因为几位客人不太会说中文。一名少年用图画和翻译软件打开话题，很快，各个家庭便开始比较学校生活、烹饪方法和童年游戏。","名单记录姓与名，目的只是方便联系而非评判。服务对象包括婴儿、青少年、待业青年和独居老人。有的家庭作为移民来到这里，有的从国外迁出，也有人只是在国内迁移。新环境和社会背景塑造了每个人的故事。","友好比赛邀请居民分享喜欢或讨厌的音乐。月光下，人们谈食欲、地毯、职业、货运、旧伤疤和冬日围巾。牧师、基督徒家庭与敬奉不同圣人的邻居共进晚餐。活动没有抹去差异，却提供了理解差异的安全方式。后来，新邻居在公寓院子里举办开放日下午活动。孩子们互相教授几乎不需要语言的游戏，成年人则交流公交、诊所和本地规定等实用信息。"]},{"day":30,"title":"The Road Through the Mountain","theme":"山区交通、安全治理与文化保护","wordCount":309,"english":["A sacred church stood on a holy hill beside fields of carrot and other root crops. Rot had damaged its wooden gate, so a carpenter rotated shifts with a carrier who brought supplies by carriage and cart. The town hoped to automate ticketing, but an automatic system still needed a reliable engine and trained engineer. Before construction, villagers marked a school route and an ambulance route that had to remain open at all times.","Engineering students compared each automobile, vehicle, motor, motel, petrol station, wagon, coach and saddle used on the mountain road. Drivers sounded a horn when a fleet met at a narrow turn. One breakdown revealed a crack in the tunnel wall. It would be wicked, even evil, to hide the danger in a busy channel. Heavy rain exposed the danger before the main work began: stones rolled onto the old road and trapped a school bus for an hour. No one was hurt, but the incident persuaded officials to fund protective barriers rather than repair only the surface.","Guides helped steer traffic while villagers applauded. Some clapped when a repair team arrived, though one impatient driver slapped his door, slipped near a loose slipper, and nearly fell down a steep slope. A dark stain marked the wet surface. Workers kept a steady pace, established a stable barrier, and prevented cars from sliding.","Strong wind could swing a sign, bend a wing mirror, sway a bus and sweep dust across the road. The event scared passengers, but the repair team stayed calm. Protecting a historic place, they learned, requires modern transport rules as well as respect for sacred memory. The road finally opened later than promised, but the delay prevented greater damage. Engineers published photographs of each repair stage, and villagers were able to see why drainage channels and stronger supports mattered more than a hurried ceremony."],"translation":["一座神圣教堂坐落在山丘上，旁边是胡萝卜等根茎作物田。腐烂损坏了木门，一名木匠与运送物资的搬运工轮班工作，物资通过马车和手推车送来。小镇想实现售票自动化，但自动系统仍需要可靠发动机和受训工程师。施工前，村民标出了必须始终保持畅通的上学路线和救护车路线。","工程专业学生比较山区道路使用的车辆、汽车旅馆、加油站、货车、长途车和马鞍。车队在狭窄弯道相遇时，司机鸣笛提示。一次故障暴露出隧道墙的裂缝；在繁忙通道隐瞒危险既恶劣又不道德。主体工程开始前，一场暴雨暴露了危险：石块滚落到旧路上，使一辆校车被困一小时。虽然无人受伤，这次事件却促使官员资助防护设施，而不是只修补路面。","向导协助引导交通，村民为维修队鼓掌。一名急躁司机拍打车门，在掉落的拖鞋旁滑倒，险些跌下陡坡。湿地面留下深色污迹。工人保持稳定节奏，设立牢固护栏，防止车辆滑行。","强风会让路牌摆动、后视镜弯折、公交摇晃，还会把灰尘扫过道路。乘客受到惊吓，维修队却保持镇定。保护历史场所既需要尊重神圣记忆，也需要现代交通规则。公路最终比承诺时间晚开放，但这次延期避免了更大的损失。工程师公布每个修复阶段的照片，村民因此看清，排水沟和坚固支撑比仓促举行通车仪式更重要。"]},{"day":31,"title":"A First-Aid Lesson Nobody Forgot","theme":"校园急救、公共健康与应急保障","wordCount":293,"english":["During a sports day, a bottle began to spill and water spread across the floor. Despite a classmate's spite, volunteers prayed that nobody would become prey to panic. They sprayed a warning mark, split the crowd into groups and formed a protective sphere around the injured runner.","A sharp stem had cut his leg. One student swore she saw a sword and arrow, but teachers collected a sample and specimen before making claims. The runner felt dizzy; bright lamps could dazzle him, and the dazzling scene made him faint. The instructor created an unexpected test by asking a volunteer to pretend to faint. Some students immediately reached for their phones, while others checked breathing and cleared the space. The class then discussed which actions truly helped.","The school had insured the event. Insurance could not assure safety, so staff ensured that every guarantee and pledge was supported by action. A nurse delivered first aid and explained how an organ, organic tissue and an organism function. The body absorbs nutrients through its intake; a straw does not replace proper hydration, and food must digest safely to avoid contagion.","A physician diagnosed the injury and said surgery was unnecessary. A surgeon, physicist and physics teacher later discussed medical imaging and a safe dose. Volunteers bundled supplies, restored order and helped the runner recover. His recovery and healing showed why preparation is the best remedy. In a final language review, the class also used swear, swell, organize, organization and physical accurately in context. A month later, one student used the lesson when a customer collapsed in a café. She called for help, followed the correct steps and stayed calm until medical workers arrived. Her classmates then reviewed the event without turning it into a heroic story."],"translation":["运动会上一只瓶子漏水，水洒遍地面。志愿者不理会同学的恶意，祈祷没人因恐慌受害。他们喷出警示标记，把人群分组，并围成保护圈。","尖锐的植物茎划伤了跑步者。有人发誓看见刀剑和箭，但教师先收集样本再判断。伤者头晕，耀眼灯光可能让他昏倒。教练安排了一次意外测试，让一名志愿者假装晕倒。有些学生立刻拿出手机，另一些人则检查呼吸并清理周围空间。随后，全班讨论了哪些行动真正有帮助。","学校为活动投保，但保险不能自动保证安全，所有承诺都要靠行动实现。护士实施急救，并讲解器官、组织与生命体怎样运作，以及吸收、摄入和消化的重要性。","医生诊断后认为无需手术。外科医生、物理学家与教师随后介绍影像和安全剂量。志愿者收好物资、恢复秩序，帮助伤者康复。准备充分才是最好的补救。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。一个月后，一名学生在咖啡馆遇到顾客倒地时用上了所学知识。她呼救、按正确步骤处理，并冷静等到医护人员到场。此后同学复盘事件，却没有把它夸张成英雄故事。"]},{"day":32,"title":"Giving an Old Hall a New Purpose","theme":"公益捐赠、文化空间与心理支持","wordCount":303,"english":["A town planned to inject new life into an abandoned hall. The subject was difficult: residents viewed the building as an object of memory, while critics might reject the project or eject its organisers. Planners anticipated objections and invited everyone to participate. A public notice also explained how groups could book rooms without excluding smaller organisations.","An antique dealer agreed to donate furniture and devote time to repair. Volunteers dedicated themselves to delicate work, contributed tools and distributed tasks. No one sought retribution for old disputes; the team treated patience as an attribute it owed the community. Architects first wanted to remove the worn stage, but former performers showed that it had excellent sound. Repairing it cost less than replacing it and preserved memories that mattered to the neighbourhood, so the stage became the centre of the new plan.","They combined art with counselling. The combination connected neighbours, created a conjunction of services and strengthened social cohesion. A joint plan integrated education without letting any group disintegrate. Tangible results came through direct contact: the roof remained intact, pictures were attached securely, and loose paper would cling or stick only with safe, non-sticky cement and glue. Each clue and cue guided visitors. Local residents were invited to propose uses for the hall. Teenagers wanted rehearsal rooms, older people requested daytime classes, and parents needed a safe place for children after school. The final timetable shared the building among them.","The mayor commended the plan and recommended a quiet room where people could relax their nerves, become calm and discuss bitter experiences, misery and sorrow. Attendance was not compulsory, even when talking was painful. The renewed hall showed that practical repair and emotional care can support one another. In a final language review, the class also used remedy, phenomenon, owe and bit accurately in context."],"translation":["小镇计划为废弃礼堂注入新生命。建筑既是记忆对象，也可能遭到反对，规划者因此预先邀请居民参与。一份公开说明还解释了各团体如何预订房间，同时不排挤较小的组织。","古董商捐赠家具并投入修缮。志愿者专心完成精细工作、贡献工具、分配任务，不因旧争端报复，而把耐心视为应尽责任。建筑师起初想拆除磨损的舞台，但老演员证明它的音响效果很好。修复比更换成本低，也能保存社区珍视的记忆，因此舞台成为新方案的中心。","项目把艺术与心理咨询结合起来，连接邻里、整合服务并增强凝聚力。屋顶保持完好，图片牢固安装，黏合材料也安全使用。每条线索和提示都帮助访客。当地居民受邀为大厅提出用途。青少年希望有排练室，老年人需要日间课程，家长则需要孩子放学后的安全活动场所。最终时间表让不同人群共享这座建筑。","市长称赞方案，并建议设置安静房间，让人放松神经、平静谈论痛苦经历。参与并非强制，即使交流有时令人难受。实际修缮与情感关怀可以相互支持。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。"]},{"day":33,"title":"The Documentary Behind the Numbers","theme":"校园调查、媒体表达与公共讨论","wordCount":297,"english":["A student felt despair after comparing her film with a professional documentary. In desperation she became desperate and worked desperately, trying to accelerate editing without knowing when to decelerate. She exaggerated every groan and filmed an actor crawling like a cartoon figure. The filmmakers followed one family for an entire year rather than collecting a few emotional scenes. They recorded ordinary bills, working hours and school journeys, then asked economists to explain what the numbers could and could not prove.","Her teacher asked the team to portray people honestly. A portrait of one street gang should not label every flock, band or neighbourhood. A first-aid bandage and a holiday resort could both appear, but each image needed context. Students classified sources as classic, recent or unreliable. One draft even used the misspelling upgrate; they corrected it to upgrade.","The final film examined a public battle over a sports ground. It did not beat viewers with dramatic claims or depict citizens as beasts in combat. Interviews showed a hammer striking a fence, one angry punch, a formal debate and a continuing dispute. A quiet hint could demonstrate more than a slogan.","The democratic meeting was illustrated with a short demo. Evidence could imply bias, whether implicit or explicit, but the film had to convey findings through a survey. Students learned how families invest, investigated investment decisions, and documented the investigation with statistics, and asked for consent before presenting or representing anyone. The careful process turned disappointment into responsible journalism. In a final language review, the class also used hit and resent accurately in context. At the first screening, the family watched the film before the public did. They requested two changes where editing had made their choices look simpler than they were. The filmmakers accepted both and described the revisions during the discussion."],"translation":["一名学生把自己的影片与专业纪录片比较后陷入绝望。她拼命加速剪辑，却不知何时放慢，还夸大呻吟声，把演员拍得像爬行的卡通人物。摄制组没有只收集几个煽情镜头，而是跟拍一个家庭整整一年。他们记录日常账单、工作时间和上学路程，再请经济学家说明这些数字能够证明什么、不能证明什么。","教师要求诚实描绘人物。一个街头团伙不能代表所有群体。绷带和度假地都可入镜，但必须有背景。学生把资料分为经典、近期与不可靠类别，并把误拼的 upgrate 改为 upgrade。","成片调查一场运动场争议，不用戏剧化说法打击观众，也不把市民描写成野兽。镜头包含锤击围栏、一次挥拳、正式辩论和持续争端；安静线索有时比口号更有说服力。","影片用简短演示呈现民主会议，通过调查传达隐性或显性偏见。学生核查投资、用统计记录调查，并在展示或代表他人前取得同意。认真过程把失望变成负责任的新闻实践。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。首次放映时，这个家庭比公众先观看影片。他们要求修改两处内容，因为剪辑使他们的选择看起来过于简单。摄制组接受了两项意见，并在讨论中说明修改过程。"]},{"day":34,"title":"The Embassy Open Day","theme":"国际交流、应急互助与青年成长","wordCount":293,"english":["A student representative spoke on behalf of classmates who were absent from an embassy open day. She arrived punctually, although a storm had postponed the postman's delivery of postage and postcards. A delay did not stop staff from ascertaining identities, certifying documents and checking each certificate, license and diploma.","A young diplomat explained diplomacy at the embassy. He admitted an embarrassing packing mistake: one packet and parcel were wrapped in a towel instead of placed under the tower's protective veil. Staff unveiled the box, removed its mask and found tissue, baggage and emergency supplies rather than anything evil. One diplomat described a failed project rather than a success. His honesty surprised the audience and led to better questions about cultural misunderstanding, public spending and the slow work of building trust.","The load was a burden for vulnerable and feeble travellers, so volunteers handled it with tender care. Mild weather turned wild, making people tremble and shiver. An aid group received an award and reward for calm service, even when communication became awkward. The most popular room was not the formal reception hall but a small language corner. Visitors wrote questions on cards, diplomats answered without prepared speeches, and students compared how the same international problem was reported in several countries.","Visitors stood in awe of brilliant rescue work. The storm looked awful, yet the response was terrific, magnificent and spectacular. Students marvelled at the grand cooperation, called the volunteers fabulous, and learned that public service is not fabricated praise. It is careful work performed when others need help. Before leaving, visitors wrote one assumption that the day had changed. Some had expected only ceremony and formal language; instead, they found ordinary workers discussing visas, disaster relief and student exchanges in direct, practical terms."],"translation":["学生代表为缺席同学参加使馆开放日。她准时到达，尽管暴风雨推迟了邮差运送邮资材料和明信片。工作人员仍核实身份、证明文件并检查证书、执照和文凭。","年轻外交官介绍使馆工作，也承认一次尴尬打包错误：包裹被毛巾裹着，而非放在塔楼保护帘后。工作人员拆开后发现的是纸巾、行李和应急用品。一位外交人员讲述的不是成功项目，而是一次失败经历。他的坦诚令听众意外，也引出了有关文化误解、公共支出以及如何慢慢建立信任的更深入问题。","物资对身体脆弱的旅客是负担，志愿者便温和照料。天气由和缓转为猛烈，人们发抖发冷。援助团队即使沟通不顺，仍因冷静服务获奖。最受欢迎的不是正式接待厅，而是一个小小的语言角。参观者把问题写在卡片上，外交人员不用讲稿直接回答，学生则比较同一国际问题在不同国家如何被报道。","访客敬佩出色救援。风暴可怕，应对却极为精彩。学生赞叹大规模合作，并明白公共服务不是编造赞美，而是在他人需要时认真行动。离开前，参观者写下一项当天改变的原有看法。有些人原以为只有仪式和正式语言，却看到普通工作人员以直接、实际的方式讨论签证、灾害救援和学生交流。"]},{"day":35,"title":"Threads of Trust","theme":"纺织产业、营养健康与商业道德","wordCount":303,"english":["A coastal workshop used fabric, fibre and traditional methods to weave cloth whose pattern moved like a wave and tide. Workers kept the floor tidy and discussed vitamin and nutrition needs. Noise was a nuisance, while rigid shifts, harsh words and cruel or brutal treatment could leave both a bruise and a deeper wound.","Managers learned that a dependant worker still deserved respect, and an independent voice could protect safety. A company's reputation, prestige and fame should rest on fair practice. A famous brand gains esteem only when its esteemed leaders remain faithful to their stated faith and loyal to employees. The cooperative began after two workshops accused each other of copying a pattern. Instead of going to court, the owners displayed their records, identified a design both families had used for decades, and agreed to share its history publicly.","The town's royal history included a noble queen, a crown, a long queue and regal ceremonies. Yet modern leadership had to be upright in a moral rather than merely vertical sense. Merit and virtue mattered more than rank. Young designers then visited both workshops and recorded the makers' techniques. Their exhibition named every contributor, showed where materials came from and explained how cooperation protected the craft from cheap imitation.","The factory rejected violent discipline and any act that would violate rights or isolate workers. New staff learned to navigate machines and notice a dangerous vibration. Via regular meetings, managers gave considerable consideration to considerate suggestions. A safety plan was not a fancy fantasy or fascinating illusion; it was evidence that dignity and production can coexist. Sales improved after the exhibition, but the partners limited production so that training and quality would not suffer. A portion of the income funded apprenticeships, giving young residents a reason to learn the craft without copying it mechanically."],"translation":["海滨作坊用布料、纤维和传统方法织布，纹样像海浪与潮汐。工人保持地面整洁，并讨论维生素与营养。噪声令人烦恼，僵化班次、严厉言语和残酷对待都会留下身体或心理创伤。","管理者认识到，有家属负担的员工仍应受尊重，独立意见也能保障安全。企业声誉和名望必须建立在公平实践上；知名品牌只有忠实守信并忠于员工，才能赢得尊重。两家作坊互相指责对方抄袭图案，合作项目由此开始。双方没有诉诸法庭，而是展示记录，确认两家几十年来都使用过这一设计，并同意共同公开它的历史。","小镇王室历史中有贵族、女王、王冠、长队和庄严仪式，但现代领导更应在道德意义上正直。功绩与美德比地位重要。年轻设计师随后走访两家作坊，记录工匠技法。展览注明每位贡献者，展示材料来源，并说明合作怎样保护这门手艺免受廉价仿制品冲击。","工厂拒绝暴力管理和侵犯权利、孤立员工的做法。员工学习操控机器并识别危险震动。经理通过例会认真考虑体贴建议。安全计划不是幻想，而是尊严与生产可以并存的证据。展览后销量增加，但合作双方限制产量，以免培训和质量受到影响。部分收入用于学徒项目，使年轻居民有理由学习这门手艺，而不是机械模仿。"]},{"day":36,"title":"Learning to Make a Clear Claim","theme":"批判性思维、职业认识与有效表达","wordCount":306,"english":["A philosophy class began with a simple notion: a point changes when viewed from another standpoint. At a checkpoint, students checked a cheque, an image and an imagined report. Infinite questions did not prevent them from defining terms, writing a definition and reaching a definite conclusion without letting time confine them, even within the confined schedule. The lesson opened with two reports about the same event. One used emotional language and unnamed sources; the other showed dates, documents and uncertainty. Students initially preferred the first, then discovered how easily confidence could be mistaken for truth.","They refined each argument and paid a fine for no mistake; the teacher emphasized learning, not punishment. Students analysed a processional photograph and discussed profession, confession, occupation, philosopher and philosophy. Their task was to clarify a clarified statement, confirm firm evidence and affirm only what the facts supported. During peer review, classmates challenged weak assumptions but were required to suggest a clearer alternative. This rule kept criticism focused on the argument rather than the person presenting it.","Each group made a claim, proclaimed its value, reclaimed a weak idea, exclaimed at a surprise, and responded to public acclaim without declaiming dramatically. A formal declaration still needed reasons. Students could admire an admirable speaker, adore an adorable story, or feel envy and jealousy, but emotion was not proof.","Finally they applied the lesson to a job applicant. They checked whether a rule was applicable, whether an appliance was safe, and whether a reply could be relayed accurately. Clear thinking, they learned, makes communication more reliable. In a final language review, the class also used occupy and declare accurately in context. For the final exercise, students examined a popular post that sounded confident but cited no source. They separated fact from opinion, rewrote the claim in careful language, and added the evidence a reader would need before accepting it."],"translation":["哲学课从一个简单观念开始：同一点从不同立场观察会不同。在检查点，学生核对支票、图片和设想的报告。无限问题并未阻止他们定义术语、写出定义并在有限时间内得出明确结论。课程以关于同一事件的两篇报道开始。一篇使用情绪化语言和匿名来源，另一篇则提供日期、文件并承认不确定性。学生起初更喜欢第一篇，随后发现自信的语气多么容易被误认为事实。","课堂完善论证，强调学习而非处罚。学生分析仪式队伍照片，讨论职业、坦白、哲学家等概念。他们澄清陈述、确认可靠证据，只肯定事实支持的内容。同伴互评时，同学可以质疑薄弱假设，但必须提出更清楚的替代说法。这项规则让批评集中于论点，而不是提出论点的人。","各组提出并公开主张，修正薄弱想法，对意外表示惊讶，也不因公众赞誉而夸张朗诵。正式声明仍需理由。人们可以欣赏优秀演说者或可爱故事，也会嫉妒，但情绪不是证据。","最后，学生把方法用于求职者案例，检查规则是否适用、电器是否安全、答复能否准确转达。他们明白，清晰思考让沟通更可靠。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。最后的练习要求学生分析一条语气肯定却没有注明来源的热门帖子。他们区分事实与观点，用谨慎语言重写主张，并补充读者在接受结论前所需的证据。"]},{"day":37,"title":"A Convenient App for a Real Emergency","theme":"数字工具、灾害应对与公共服务","wordCount":308,"english":["A reliable and credible emergency app could be convenient without making authorities liable for every choice. Designers studied legal liability, how users tend to act, and their tendency to follow a trend. They extended the test, stretched its range and ran extensive trials attended by residents.","Some developers contended that speed mattered most; others intended to protect privacy. Nobody should pretend to solve every problem, disguise weak results, simulate success or stimulate panic. A small reminder could spur action without imitating an alarm. Users could tap the screen or pat a child calmly rather than react with uncontrolled passion. During a real storm, however, the app sent too many warnings and confused users. The design team watched how families actually responded, removed unnecessary steps and added an offline guide for people whose internet connection had failed.","The team was keen to include handwriting for people who found keyboards less handy. To convince doubtful officials, diligent workers tested routes to every destination, including a labour district hit by disaster, famine and a volcano warning. Vague or dim maps caused distress and could restrict rescue. Engineers also discovered that convenience could create risk. If location data were stored without limits, the system might reveal when a family had left home. The privacy setting was therefore made visible and easy to change.","Designers removed disgusting images that might disgust or disturb users. A clear dimension and column layout helped people draft a message while a rescue boat drifted, floated and dropped anchor near an injured ankle. Technology served the public only when human needs shaped the design. In a final language review, the class also used intention, convenience and labor accurately in context. The revised app was tested with older residents, international students and people with hearing difficulties. Their feedback changed the size of buttons, the wording of alerts and the use of sound."],"translation":["可靠可信的应急应用应当方便使用，却不能让部门为每个个人选择承担责任。设计者研究法律责任和用户追随趋势的倾向，扩大测试并邀请居民参加广泛试用。","有人认为速度最重要，另一些人重视隐私。团队不能假装解决一切、掩饰薄弱结果、模拟成功或制造恐慌。轻微提醒即可推动行动，无需模仿警报；用户应冷静点击屏幕或安抚孩子。然而，在一次真实暴风雨中，应用发送了过多警报，反而让用户困惑。设计团队观察家庭的实际反应，删除不必要步骤，并为断网用户增加离线指南。","团队加入手写功能，方便不习惯键盘的人。勤奋成员测试通往各目的地的路线，包括遭遇灾害、饥荒或火山警报的劳动者社区。模糊地图会造成痛苦并限制救援。工程师还发现，便利也可能带来风险。如果位置数据被无限期保存，系统可能暴露某个家庭何时离家。因此，隐私设置被设计得清楚可见且容易更改。","设计者删除令人不适的画面，采用清晰尺寸与栏目布局，帮助用户起草信息。救援船漂流后在脚踝受伤者附近下锚。只有人的需求塑造设计，技术才真正服务公众。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。改进后的应用由老年居民、留学生和听力困难者共同测试。他们的反馈改变了按钮大小、警报措辞和声音的使用方式。"]},{"day":38,"title":"Explaining Space Science to Everyone","theme":"航天科普、科学传播与团队协作","wordCount":302,"english":["A science editor prepared a new version of an exhibition, from the atom and electron to electricity, an astronaut and a satellite. Nuclear topics required careful language. Visitors could respond through a survey; each respondent received a reply, and staff would correspond with schools and use feedback in the next phase. Instead of beginning with formulas, the guide began with the history of one photograph. That story gave visitors a reason to care before they met the difficult science behind it.","Every phrase and profile had to be accurate. A spontaneous question might reveal confusion, while a sponsor could support better displays. Because fatigue and exhaust from nearby traffic made guides exhausted and weary, the museum expanded rest areas and chose a feasible schedule.","A feather experiment introduced air resistance and character in scientific writing. Each file and document was checked so nobody could forge results. A fortnight of tests covered a wide range of ages, and staff arranged each event until the final day. The exhibition included a scale model that visitors could touch and a dark room that reproduced the night sky. Children asked direct questions, and researchers discovered that a clear comparison often explained more than a page of technical terms.","Eventually, the exhibition explained consequence and sequence through a series and chain of demonstrations. Subsequent reviews occurred frequently; secondary details supported the primary and prime message, while preliminary models showed how primitive tools led to modern science. Questions did not offend guides, who defended open inquiry. In a final language review, the class also used drum, consequently and subsequently accurately in context. After the exhibition, teachers received a small kit for repeating the activities in class. It included questions rather than a prepared lecture, encouraging pupils to make predictions, test models and explain what evidence changed their minds."],"translation":["科学编辑准备新版展览，从原子、电子和电讲到宇航员与卫星。核能话题需要谨慎语言。访客通过问卷回应，工作人员与学校通信并把反馈用于下一阶段。讲解员没有从公式讲起，而是先介绍一张照片的历史。这个故事让参观者在接触背后的复杂科学之前，先产生了关心它的理由。","每个短语和人物介绍都要准确。自发问题可能暴露困惑，赞助者则支持改进展示。交通废气和疲劳让讲解员十分劳累，博物馆因此扩大休息区并制定可行日程。","羽毛实验介绍空气阻力，也训练科学写作。每份文件都经核查，防止伪造结果。两周测试覆盖不同年龄，活动一直安排到最终日。展览设置了可触摸的比例模型和模拟夜空的暗室。孩子们提出直接的问题，研究人员发现，一个清楚的类比往往比一页专业术语更能说明问题。","展览用一系列相连实验解释后果与顺序。后续审查频繁进行，次要细节服务主要信息，初步模型则展示原始工具如何走向现代科学。提问不会冒犯讲解员，他们捍卫开放探究。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。展览结束后，教师获得一套可在课堂重复活动的小工具。材料提供的是问题而非现成讲稿，鼓励学生作出预测、测试模型，并说明什么证据改变了自己的想法。"]},{"day":39,"title":"Homes Worth More Than Their Price","theme":"住房权益、社区治理与问题解决","wordCount":297,"english":["A fence separated an empty estate from families seeking appropriate housing. Officials debated propriety and property: who should possess the land, who held possession and ownership, and whether private wealth made the site worth more than its worthwhile public use. The land was an asset, but high prices upset residents. The housing study began when rents rose sharply near the university. Researchers visited new towers and older streets, measured travel time and heating costs, and asked residents which features made a dwelling feel like a secure home.","A fair settlement allowed families to settle and dwell in safe dwellings. Managers learned to handle complaints, tackle repairs, solve disputes and resolve them through a written resolution. Unsafe paint could dissolve, so staff addressed it quickly.","The project looked giant and its cost gigantic, immense, tremendous and vast. Yet normal checks found no abnormal or enormous danger. Architects used precise but concise language, keeping plans simple while explaining subtle and extreme risks with the utmost honesty. They did not utter utterly false claims or rely on sheer authority. The report therefore ranked homes by several measures, not price alone. It included access to buses, sunlight, noise, repair quality and the risk that a sudden rent increase would force a family to move.","Affordable housing was an absolute possibility, not an impossible dream, if probable costs were separated from abstract fear. A tractor could subtract old soil, workers could deduct waste, reduce expense and extract reusable stone. Public value grew when the town treated housing as both property and home. Officials used the findings to revise a student-housing guide. It now warned that a low monthly rent could be offset by long travel and poor insulation, and it gave tenants a checklist for inspecting a room before paying a deposit."],"translation":["一道围栏把空置地产与需要住房的家庭隔开。官员讨论财产与适当原则：谁占有土地、谁有所有权，私人财富是否比公共用途更有价值。土地是资产，高价却让居民不安。这项住房研究始于大学附近租金大幅上涨之时。研究人员走访新建高楼和老街区，测量通勤时间与取暖费用，并询问居民哪些条件能让住所真正带来安全感。","公平协议让家庭安顿在安全住宅中。管理者处理投诉、解决维修和争端，并写入正式决议。危险油漆可能溶解，工作人员迅速处理。","项目规模巨大、成本高昂，但常规检查并未发现异常巨大风险。建筑师用准确简洁语言说明细微和极端风险，不说虚假话，也不只靠权威。因此，报告没有只按价格评价住房，而是采用多项指标，包括公交便利、采光、噪声、维修质量，以及租金突然上涨迫使家庭搬家的风险。","经济住房并非不可能。拖拉机移走旧土，工人扣除废料、降低开支并提取可再用石材。小镇把住房同时视为财产与家园时，公共价值便提高了。有关部门根据调查结果修改了学生住房指南。新版提醒人们，较低月租可能被漫长通勤和糟糕保温抵消，并为租客提供付押金前检查房间的清单。"]},{"day":40,"title":"The True Cost of a Cheap Product","theme":"理性消费、产品价值与可持续选择","wordCount":307,"english":["A bright advertisement can attract buyers, but an attractive package may distract them from a contract. Reliable information should be available and prevail over prevailing fashion. A stiff or clumsy product is less useful than a flexible one that can reflect real needs. Elastic and plastic parts also differ in whether they are permanent or seem eternal. The investigation began with a challenge from a local retailer: could students prove that a cheap product caused harm? Instead of assuming the answer, they followed documents, interviewed workers and compared several suppliers.","A consumer class compared double, duple and multiple packs, a couple of samples, a single item and a singular design. Regular shopping is not merely about finding the sole lowest price. Students learned to evaluate what was valuable, avoid claims that devalue labour, and notice when firms undervalue repair.","They calculated expenditure: to expend more on an expensive item may reduce later expense, while a cheap but costly failure creates waste. Each incident and its incidence were marked on a map. A weak spot might have potential to cause harm on a special occasion, during occasional use or through casual neglect. Students traced one cheap shirt from the cotton field to the shop. The low price looked attractive, but water use, transport, unsafe labour and unsold stock created costs that never appeared on the label.","The best opportunity came from transparent communication. Companies transmitted data, omitted no major fault, explained their mission without missionary pressure, dismissed false claims, and distinguished a missile warning from ordinary emissions. Buyers could submit questions and admit uncertainty. Honest information made choice easier. In a final language review, the class also used emit accurately in context. The class did not demand that everyone stop shopping. It proposed buying fewer but longer-lasting clothes, repairing damaged items and asking retailers to publish supply information."],"translation":["明亮广告能吸引买家，漂亮包装也会分散人们对合同的注意。可靠信息应压过流行风尚。僵硬笨重的产品不如能反映真实需求的灵活产品；弹性与塑料零件也要考虑是否耐久。调查源于本地零售商提出的挑战：学生能否证明廉价产品造成了伤害？他们没有预设答案，而是追查文件、采访工人并比较多家供应商。","课堂比较双份、多份、成对、单件与特殊设计。日常购物不只是寻找最低价。学生学习评估价值，避免贬低劳动，也注意企业是否低估维修。","他们计算支出：昂贵耐用品可能减少后续费用，便宜却易坏的商品反而代价高。事故及发生率被标在地图上，薄弱点可能在特定场合或随意忽视中造成伤害。学生追踪了一件廉价衬衫从棉田到商店的全过程。低价看似诱人，但用水、运输、不安全劳动和滞销库存造成的代价从未出现在标签上。","企业应传送完整数据，不遗漏重大缺陷，说明使命而不强迫推销，驳斥虚假说法并区分真正警报与普通排放。消费者可以提问并承认不确定。诚实信息让选择更容易。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。班级并未要求所有人停止购物，而是建议少买一些但选择更耐穿的衣物、修补破损物品，并要求零售商公开供应链信息。"]},{"day":41,"title":"Protecting a Town's Digital Memory","theme":"数字安全、文化创新与公共管理","wordCount":290,"english":["A public commission formed a committee and committed funds to digital safety. Its work covered suicide-prevention contacts, pesticide records and a summit on mountain ecology. At the peak and climax of the meeting, experts explained altitude sensors, password protection and computer code.","Rules would regulate access, but regulation had to remain regular and fair. Officials learned to relate each related record to a relationship and a relative risk through a clear narrative. Staff narrated cases, crossed out errors and replaced weak passwords. The loss was discovered when a retired teacher asked for a photograph of the town's first school. Volunteers found that several files had been stored in outdated formats and that no one person understood the whole archive.","Engineers soaked damaged paper, tested how ink could penetrate a filter and did not hesitate to compensate owners. A candidate demonstrated a candle alarm, cancelled an unsafe canteen device, and chased no publicity. The library purchased software and pursued a long-term plan. Specialists warned that preservation was not a one-time rescue. File formats, equipment and staff would continue to change. The town therefore added an annual check and trained students to help, turning maintenance into a shared civic task.","A local legend inspired students to innovate. Their innovation supported building renovation, while myths and mysteries became material for a novel, essay, romance and romantic fiction. Designers reduced digital friction and prevented online insult. After consulting experts from another continent, the town matched ambition with careful protection. In a final language review, the class also used whistle accurately in context. The rescue team copied surviving material into open formats, stored it in more than one place and wrote simple instructions for future volunteers. Residents were also invited to identify unnamed people in old photographs."],"translation":["公共委员会投入资金保障数字安全，工作涉及预防自杀联络、农药记录和高山生态峰会。会议高潮时，专家介绍海拔传感器、密码保护与代码。","规定管理访问权限，但执行必须稳定公平。官员把各种关系与相对风险联系，用叙事串联记录，删除错误并更换弱密码。一位退休教师索要小镇第一所学校的照片时，人们才发现资料已经丢失。志愿者发现，一些文件采用过时格式保存，而且没有任何一个人了解完整档案。","工程师处理受潮纸张，测试墨水穿过滤纸的情况，并补偿物主。候选人展示蜡烛警报器，取消不安全食堂设备，不追逐宣传。图书馆购买软件并实施长期计划。专家提醒，保存资料不是一次性的抢救行动。文件格式、设备和人员都会继续变化。因此，小镇增加年度检查并培训学生参与，使维护成为共同的公共任务。","地方传说激励学生创新，支持建筑翻新；神话与谜团也成为小说、随笔和爱情故事素材。设计降低数字摩擦、防止网络侮辱，并在咨询另一大陆专家后，让雄心与保护相匹配。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。抢救小组把幸存资料转换为开放格式，分别存放在多个地点，并为未来志愿者编写简单说明。居民还受邀辨认老照片中没有姓名的人物。"]},{"day":42,"title":"One Difficult Day at the Airport","theme":"航空出行、公共健康与身份核验","wordCount":299,"english":["An orchestra played a quiet tune in an airport terminal, but passengers soon needed patience. A patented luggage brand had attached the wrong label and tag, causing bags to lag behind the normal pace. One household, including a housewife travelling with children, waited beside a garage-like service area as the information gap caused rage. The difficulty began with a delayed flight and became worse when the boarding gate changed twice. Families rushed across the terminal while a traveller using crutches struggled to keep up.","A generous host calmed the family, while a hostile customer showed open hostility. Staff offered a glove to a child with a sore hand and a tablet or pill for a traveller's headache. An ambulance remained ready, though a dramatic headline wrongly claimed that headquarters faced a crisis.","Within a quarter hour, the craft team checked every aircraft, airline flight, helicopter and jet. Aviation staff, a pilot and a dentist travelling as a passenger helped identify identical bags. Identity documents made each owner identifiable, and the error began to decline. Airport staff later replayed the incident with everyone involved. The passenger understood why the gate could not reopen, while employees admitted that repeated announcements had given conflicting instructions. A revised message was tested the next morning.","The terminal manager resisted the incline toward blame and asked people to worship no company image. Travel hardship revealed a weak wire and other shortcomings; engineers repaired it before it could weaken the system. Calm identification, not anger, returned every bag. In a final language review, the class also used terminator accurately in context. The airport also changed how it assisted travellers with limited mobility. Instead of asking them to request help again after every gate change, one staff member remained responsible until they boarded or chose another flight."],"translation":["机场航站楼里，管弦乐队演奏轻柔曲调，乘客却很快需要耐心。某专利行李品牌贴错标签，行李落后于正常运送速度。一个家庭在类似车库的服务区等待，信息缺口引发愤怒。问题始于航班延误，登机口两次变更后情况更加糟糕。许多家庭匆忙穿过航站楼，一名拄拐旅客却难以跟上。","慷慨的接待员安抚家人，一名敌意顾客却公开发火。工作人员给手部疼痛的孩子提供手套，也为头痛旅客提供药片。救护车随时待命，但夸张标题错误宣称总部陷入危机。","十五分钟内，机务人员核查各种飞机、航班和直升机。一名飞行员与恰好在场的牙医协助辨认相同行李，身份证明让物主可以确认，错误逐渐减少。机场工作人员事后与所有相关人员一起复盘。旅客理解了登机口为何不能重新开放，员工也承认多次广播给出了相互矛盾的指示。第二天早晨，新的通知内容接受了测试。","经理不再相互责怪。出行困难暴露出电线和其他缺点，工程师及时修复。最终让每件行李归位的是冷静核验，而不是愤怒。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。机场还改变了帮助行动不便旅客的方式。登机口每次变更后，不再要求旅客重新求助，而是由同一名工作人员负责，直到他们登机或改乘其他航班。"]},{"day":43,"title":"A Picnic That Challenged Prejudice","theme":"校园餐饮、反对种族歧视与安全意识","wordCount":301,"english":["A community picnic faced a disadvantage, a budget drawback and a weather setback, but no obstacle could hinder volunteers. A herd in a nearby field and a pigeon on the roof made the scene animate and vivid. Organisers wanted the event to survive and revive trust among neighbours. The picnic was organised after hurtful comments appeared in a class group chat. Rather than forcing an apology, the teacher asked students to plan food and games in mixed teams so that unfamiliar classmates had a reason to cooperate.","Children painted a plain wall while adults complained about rain. Nobody plunged or dived into the river because signs warned of drowning. Cooks served pork, beef, mutton and seafood, cut every slice and chip, added onion and sauce, and shared each recipe. Guests could dine, snack, chew carefully, use a napkin, pour water and solve a food puzzle by guessing ingredients.","A discussion then addressed radical ideas, racial division, racism and racist language. A former rebel described terror that had terrified families and left dreadful memories. One listener turned pale and pressed a palm to her face. During the meal, each group introduced a dish and the memory connected with it. Students who had repeated stereotypes began to hear classmates as individuals rather than labels.","Leaders urged caution, cautious speech and practical precaution. Everyone became aware that prejudice can hide in jokes. When a storm alert sounded, the same respect guided a safe departure: people helped one another rather than dividing by background. In a final language review, the class also used lick and horror accurately in context. The class later wrote a group agreement for online discussion. It did not ban disagreement; it required students to question ideas with reasons, avoid labels and speak privately to a teacher when a message felt threatening."],"translation":["社区野餐面临不利条件、预算缺点和天气挫折，但志愿者没有被障碍阻止。附近的牲畜与屋顶鸽子让场面生动，活动希望维持并恢复邻里信任。这次野餐是在班级群里出现伤人言论后组织的。老师没有强迫学生道歉，而是让大家组成混合小组安排食物和游戏，使不熟悉的同学有机会合作。","孩子粉刷普通墙面，大人抱怨下雨。河边标志提醒溺水危险，无人下水。厨师准备多种肉类和海鲜，切片、加洋葱与酱汁并分享食谱。客人用餐、细嚼、使用餐巾、倒水，还猜测食材。","讨论随后转向激进思想、种族差异、种族主义和歧视言语。一名前反抗者讲述曾让家庭恐惧的经历，一名听众脸色苍白。用餐时，每组介绍一道食物及与它相关的记忆。曾经重复刻板印象的学生开始把同学看作具体的人，而不再只是某种标签。","主持人呼吁谨慎表达并采取预防措施。大家意识到偏见可能藏在玩笑里。风暴警报响起后，同样的尊重引导所有人安全离开，人们互相帮助，不按背景分开。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。此后，全班共同制定网络讨论约定。约定并不禁止分歧，而是要求学生用理由质疑观点、避免给人贴标签，并在信息带有威胁感时私下告诉老师。"]},{"day":44,"title":"The Office That Relearned Cooperation","theme":"职场伦理、团队沟通与公共行政","wordCount":308,"english":["A worker's conscience made her conscious of a loose screw near the crew's equipment. She warned a colleague, a fellow technician and all staff not to pile stuff nearby. One manager was tempted to hide the fault, attempted a quick fix and treated criticism with contempt, but others despised the shortcut. The office had once rewarded employees who spoke longest in meetings, even when they repeated other people's ideas. A failed project revealed the cost of that habit: two departments had noticed the same risk, but neither felt responsible for raising it clearly.","A triangle of safety officers urged action without haste or hatred. Harmony mattered more than winning a vain argument. Though two machines resembled each other, the team assembled the correct parts and showed sympathy and mercy to the employee who had erred. The manager also replaced anonymous complaints with confidential conversations led by a trained mediator. People could describe a problem safely, but they also had to take part in finding a workable solution.","An alarm symptom became a symbol of wider culture and symbolized the need for change. A wise and sane leader used wit, and likewise asked alike departments to review clockwise moving parts. A broad review gained breadth by inviting experts from abroad and overseas.","The board welcomed them aboard the project, and a panel recommended that management widen training. It protected wild areas, lengthened useful practice without making meetings lengthy, and sent findings to federal officials. Faded rules were rewritten. The ministry would govern through fair standards, administer support and improve administrative work. In a final language review, the class also used symphony and leadership accurately in context. Three months later, meetings were shorter but more useful. Staff received agendas in advance, junior workers took turns leading discussions, and disagreements were recorded with a named person responsible for the next action."],"translation":["一名员工凭良知注意到设备旁松动的螺丝，提醒同事、技术人员和全体员工不要在附近堆东西。经理一度想隐瞒问题，仓促尝试修补并轻视批评，其他人则反对这种捷径。这间办公室过去常奖励会议上发言最长的人，即使他们只是在重复别人的观点。一个失败项目暴露了这种习惯的代价：两个部门都注意到同一风险，却都没有明确提出。","安全人员敦促行动，却不急躁或怀恨。和谐比无意义争胜重要。虽然两台机器相似，团队仍组装正确零件，也同情并宽容犯错员工。经理还用受过培训的调解员主持的保密谈话取代匿名投诉。员工可以安全地说明问题，同时也必须参与寻找可行的解决方案。","警报症状成为企业文化问题的象征。理智领导用幽默化解紧张，并让相似部门检查顺时针部件。广泛审查邀请国内外专家，视野更加开阔。","董事会吸收他们加入项目，专家组建议扩大培训。方案保护野生区域、延长有效练习但不让会议冗长，并把结果交给联邦机构。过时规定得到重写，主管部门以公平标准治理、提供支持并改善行政工作。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。三个月后，会议变短了，却更加有效。员工提前收到议程，年轻职员轮流主持讨论，每项分歧也被记录下来，并明确下一步行动的负责人。"]},{"day":45,"title":"Leading with Evidence","theme":"健康教育、公共传播与理性判断","wordCount":305,"english":["Good leadership does not mislead people or misunderstand their misfortune. A leader should guide a team with a clear guideline, measure results, rank risks by degree and show them on a scale and chart. Whether distance is a centimeter or kilometer, evidence should be exact.","A health campaign compared nylon, a kettle and a wash basin before turning to alcohol, cigarettes, liquor, drunken behaviour, beer and other beverages. Average use is not automatically safe merely because it is common or commonplace. Recovery can feel like a miracle or magic, but magnetic slogans do not replace treatment. The student leader first believed that confidence meant answering every question immediately. After giving one inaccurate figure, she changed her method: she published the source, invited correction and clearly separated confirmed facts from estimates.","The town paved a roadside path, moved a warning aside and marked a bicycle lane. A critic offered criticism that was critical but fair. Residents had to comprehend costs measured in billions, and officials had to satisfy them with a satisfactory plan ready beforehand.","A former director spoke first and a later speaker challenged the so-called easy answer. Mean statistics can mean different things depending on the means used. Meanwhile, one district improved whereas another fell behind. Leaders must ask what else is needed, thereby making policy more honest. Moreover, they should explain uncertainty; furthermore, they should keep listening after the meeting ends. In a final language review, the class also used wayside accurately in context. Her team later adopted the same practice, and public questions became easier to answer because evidence had been organised before decisions were announced. By the final meeting, disagreement had not disappeared, but it had become more useful. Participants could identify which facts they shared, which predictions remained uncertain and what new information would be collected before the next decision."],"translation":["优秀领导不会误导公众，也不会误解他们的不幸。领导者应以明确指南带领团队，衡量结果，按程度排列风险，并在尺度和图表上展示。无论距离是厘米还是公里，证据都要准确。","健康活动先比较尼龙制品、水壶和洗手盆，随后讨论酒精、香烟、烈酒、醉酒、啤酒及其他饮料。某种使用方式普遍存在，并不等于安全。康复可能像奇迹或魔法，但有吸引力的口号不能代替治疗。学生负责人起初以为，自信就是立刻回答每个问题。在给出一个错误数字后，她改变了做法：公布资料来源、欢迎纠正，并明确区分已确认事实与估算数据。","小镇铺设路旁小径，移开警告牌并划出自行车道。批评者提出关键却公平的意见。居民要理解数十亿规模的成本，官员则要用事先准备好的满意方案回应。","前任主管先发言，后来者质疑所谓简单答案。平均统计会因采用的方法而具有不同含义。与此同时，一个地区改善，另一个落后。领导者必须继续追问还需要什么，从而使政策更诚实；此外还要解释不确定性，并在会议结束后继续倾听。最后，课堂还复习了相关词汇在语境中的准确用法。团队后来也采用同样做法；由于证据在公布决定前已经整理好，公众问题也更容易得到回答。到最后一次会议时，分歧并未消失，却变得更有价值。参与者能够明确哪些事实已有共识、哪些预测仍不确定，以及下一次决定前还要收集什么新信息。"]}];
